<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" modified="2026-10-13T00:00:00Z" agent="Merchant research" version="24.7.17" type="device">
  <diagram id="bucket-01" name="01 Establish and control the business">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;01 / Establish and control the business&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Become eligible to trade and keep systems, people and automation under control.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns entity/processor access, technology reliability, permissions, privacy and business continuity. Transaction fraud belongs in 07; tax recordkeeping in 08; staff cost/payment in 10.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;1A. Eligibility and activation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need a predictable route to opening, with one clear next step when someone rejects my application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Merchant onboarding / KYB / account verification&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-01.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="01.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.1.1 · My launch is ready but the payment account is not approved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See the missing requirement, responsible party and next step for my business type.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Submitted business identity, verification status and bank details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Entity documents, ownership changes, category and country requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain rejection reasons and prepare a verifiable activation checklist.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Days at each activation stage; rejection reasons; resubmissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to first live payment; launch days lost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Onboarding / account activation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Activation guidance exists; end-to-end resolution remains conditional.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Atlas / account setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Company setup and account administration workflows.&lt;br&gt;US / supported entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/atlas&quot;&gt;U01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 2/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The fintech cannot bypass underwriting, sanctions or bank approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.1-01.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.1" target="01.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.1.2 · My legal name, shop name and bank details do not match&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Resolve identity inconsistencies before repeatedly uploading documents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Submitted business identity, verification status and bank details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Entity documents, ownership changes, category and country requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain rejection reasons and prepare a verifiable activation checklist.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Name mismatches; failed bank verification; support contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; First-pass verification rate; rework hours.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Onboarding / account activation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Verification inputs help; legal identity corrections require the merchant.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Atlas / account setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Company setup and account administration workflows.&lt;br&gt;US / supported entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/atlas&quot;&gt;U01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 2/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The fintech cannot bypass underwriting, sanctions or bank approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1592" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.1-01.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.1" target="01.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.1.3 · I do not know whether my category or new country is supported&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm eligibility and required approvals before spending on expansion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Submitted business identity, verification status and bank details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Entity documents, ownership changes, category and country requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain rejection reasons and prepare a verifiable activation checklist.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Category restrictions; location/payment-method availability; rejected applications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Expansion cost committed before eligibility confirmation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Onboarding / account activation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Published onboarding scope helps; eligibility is account-specific.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Atlas / account setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Company setup and account administration workflows.&lt;br&gt;US / supported entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/atlas&quot;&gt;U01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 1/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The fintech cannot bypass underwriting, sanctions or bank approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2497" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.1-01.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.1" target="01.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.1.4 · Changing the owner, bank account or entity interrupts my trading&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand change verification and preserve a traceable transition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Submitted business identity, verification status and bank details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Entity documents, ownership changes, category and country requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain rejection reasons and prepare a verifiable activation checklist.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Pending account changes; document expiry; activation holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Downtime during business changes; time to restore access.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Onboarding / account activation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Account administration helps; uninterrupted migration is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Atlas / account setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Company setup and account administration workflows.&lt;br&gt;US / supported entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/atlas&quot;&gt;U01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 1/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The fintech cannot bypass underwriting, sanctions or bank approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3424" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.1-01.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.1" target="01.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;1B. Systems and integration&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need confidence that the business keeps working when I am not watching every connection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Payment integration / financial-system events&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-01.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="01.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.2.1 · Checkout works in a demo but live orders fail&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Validate real payment, order, notification and refund paths before launch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment requests, API errors, event IDs, timestamps and delivery attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store order IDs, inventory/ERP sync status and deployment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace failures, deduplicate events and route unresolved financial handoffs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Test/live configuration; end-to-end completion; integration errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Live defect rate; lost orders after releases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Integration docs / webhooks / AP integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Integration support exists; live configuration still needs testing.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 1/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A payment provider sees its event boundary; it cannot certify all connected systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.2-01.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.2" target="01.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.2.2 · A delayed or repeated event creates the wrong order status&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Process each payment event reliably and resolve missing updates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment requests, API errors, event IDs, timestamps and delivery attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store order IDs, inventory/ERP sync status and deployment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace failures, deduplicate events and route unresolved financial handoffs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Webhook retries; event age; duplicate order/payment references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unmatched events; duplicate fulfillment; correction time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Integration docs / webhooks / AP integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Event handling enables recovery; merchant-side deduplication matters.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A payment provider sees its event boundary; it cannot certify all connected systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.2-01.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.2" target="01.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.2.3 · My store, stock tool and finance tool disagree after a sync fails&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Know which connection is stale and recover without overwriting good data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment requests, API errors, event IDs, timestamps and delivery attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store order IDs, inventory/ERP sync status and deployment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace failures, deduplicate events and route unresolved financial handoffs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Last sync; failed jobs; conflicting identifiers; data freshness.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Hours with stale data; manual repairs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Integration docs / webhooks / AP integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;ERP links cover some finance handoffs, not every stock system.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A payment provider sees its event boundary; it cannot certify all connected systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.2-01.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.2" target="01.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.2.4 · I depend on a developer for every payment or workflow change&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make supported changes with clear previews, testing and rollback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment requests, API errors, event IDs, timestamps and delivery attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store order IDs, inventory/ERP sync status and deployment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace failures, deduplicate events and route unresolved financial handoffs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Change backlog; configuration errors; agency turnaround.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time and cost per safe change.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Integration docs / webhooks / AP integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hosted and configured flows reduce effort; custom changes remain.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A payment provider sees its event boundary; it cannot certify all connected systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3512" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.2-01.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.2" target="01.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;1C. Roles and accountable delegation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I want to delegate routine work without handing over control of all my money and customer data.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Account permissions / payment approvals&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-01.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="01.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.3.1 · Staff share the owner login because roles are inconvenient&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Give each person only the permissions required for their work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Users, roles, approval queues and recorded financial actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Employment status, agency contracts, delegated limits and escalation contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recommend least-privilege access and route time-sensitive approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Shared logins; broad roles; owner-only bottlenecks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unauthorized changes; approval waiting time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Dashboard roles / AP approvals / agent controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Separate roles reduce shared login dependence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Teams and roles&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Scoped dashboard access and team administration.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Revoking one account does not revoke every external credential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.3-01.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.3" target="01.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.3.2 · An employee or agency leaves but still has access&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Revoke access across tools and reassign unfinished work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Users, roles, approval queues and recorded financial actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Employment status, agency contracts, delegated limits and escalation contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recommend least-privilege access and route time-sensitive approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Inactive users; unrevoked keys; orphaned tasks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to remove access; unattended work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Dashboard roles / AP approvals / agent controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Removal of provider access is supported; external offboarding remains.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Teams and roles&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Scoped dashboard access and team administration.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Revoking one account does not revoke every external credential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1570" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.3-01.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.3" target="01.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.3.3 · I cannot tell who changed an offer, refund or bank detail&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Keep a readable record of actor, reason, time and approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Users, roles, approval queues and recorded financial actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Employment status, agency contracts, delegated limits and escalation contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recommend least-privilege access and route time-sensitive approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Audit logs; configuration changes; action ownership.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Investigation time; unexplained changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Dashboard roles / AP approvals / agent controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Some controls/logs exist; one audit trail for every action is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Teams and roles&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Scoped dashboard access and team administration.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Revoking one account does not revoke every external credential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2497" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.3-01.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.3" target="01.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.3.4 · An approval is stuck because only I can authorize it&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Delegate bounded decisions and route genuine exceptions to a backup.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Users, roles, approval queues and recorded financial actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Employment status, agency contracts, delegated limits and escalation contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recommend least-privilege access and route time-sensitive approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Approval queue age; absence schedules; threshold breaches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Decision turnaround; overdue approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Dashboard roles / AP approvals / agent controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AP has multi-layer approvals; governance still defines delegates.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Teams and roles&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Scoped dashboard access and team administration.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/teams&quot;&gt;F12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Revoking one account does not revoke every external credential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3424" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.3-01.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.3" target="01.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;1D. Data permission and customer trust&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know what a tool is using and be able to withdraw access without losing my business history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Financial-data consent / connected apps&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-01.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="01.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.4.1 · I do not understand which customer data a new agent can read&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See the data sources, fields, purpose and permission scope before enabling it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Provider-held records, access scopes and authorization events where exposed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent records across marketing tools, contracts, retention and model-training terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Show a data-access ledger and propagate permitted revocation requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Connected accounts; requested scopes; data lineage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Permission comprehension; unnecessary access removed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio guardrails / connected data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Merchant-scoped controls are described; a complete data-access view needs checking.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 3/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 3/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Service processing, sharing, retention and model training are distinct permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.4-01.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.4" target="01.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.4.2 · A customer opts out in one tool but another keeps messaging&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Carry communication preferences across every active workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Provider-held records, access scopes and authorization events where exposed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent records across marketing tools, contracts, retention and model-training terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Show a data-access ledger and propagate permitted revocation requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Consent records; suppressions; conflicting customer identifiers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Messages after opt-out; complaint rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio guardrails / connected data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Agent communication checks exist; cross-tool opt-out synchronization is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 1/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 1/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Service processing, sharing, retention and model training are distinct permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.4-01.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.4" target="01.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.4.3 · I cannot distinguish using my data for my business from model training&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Get explicit product-specific answers about processing, retention and training use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Provider-held records, access scopes and authorization events where exposed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent records across marketing tools, contracts, retention and model-training terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Show a data-access ledger and propagate permitted revocation requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Contracts; privacy notices; settings; provider responses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unresolved data-use questions before activation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Agent Studio guardrails / connected data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Guardrail material does not settle all training and retention terms.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 1/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 1/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Service processing, sharing, retention and model training are distinct permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.4-01.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.4" target="01.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.4.4 · A vendor change leaves my customer records and history trapped&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Export usable records and preserve consent and transaction links.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Provider-held records, access scopes and authorization events where exposed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent records across marketing tools, contracts, retention and model-training terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Show a data-access ledger and propagate permitted revocation requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Export completeness; stable IDs; migration errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Migration downtime; records lost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio guardrails / connected data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Connected records help; complete portability across vendors is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Setu 2/5 — Account Aggregator gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Consent and financial-data fetch infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://setu.co/credit-infrastructure/credit-intelligence/account-aggregator-api&quot;&gt;F21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 2/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Service processing, sharing, retention and model training are distinct permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.4-01.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.4" target="01.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;1E. Safe automation and continuity&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need a reliable fallback and freedom to stop an automation without stopping the whole business.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Agent execution / financial continuity&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-01.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="01.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.5.1 · An AI recommendation sounds confident but uses stale or wrong facts&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See the source, timestamp and uncertainty before trusting the answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Inputs, action logs, permissions, statuses and failure codes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Source freshness, business exceptions, fallback owners and recovery procedures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Require evidence-linked recommendations, action limits and a human fallback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Source freshness; conflicting totals; unsupported claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Wrong recommendations accepted; correction time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / RazorpayX agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Conversational summaries need source freshness and calculation checks.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Logs and approvals reduce risk but do not establish guaranteed accuracy or uptime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.5-01.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.5" target="01.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.5.2 · An agent acts beyond the amount or task I intended&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Define allowed actions, money limits, review gates and immediate pause.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Inputs, action logs, permissions, statuses and failure codes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Source freshness, business exceptions, fallback owners and recovery procedures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Require evidence-linked recommendations, action limits and a human fallback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Scope violations; amount thresholds; action logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Blocked unsafe actions; unwanted actions executed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / RazorpayX agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scoped actions and approval controls are described; rollout varies.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Logs and approvals reduce risk but do not establish guaranteed accuracy or uptime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.5-01.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.5" target="01.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.5.3 · Automation fails halfway and nobody owns the remaining work&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See partial completion, safe retry state and a named human handoff.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Inputs, action logs, permissions, statuses and failure codes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Source freshness, business exceptions, fallback owners and recovery procedures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Require evidence-linked recommendations, action limits and a human fallback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Failed actions; retry count; unresolved queue age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to recover; duplicate actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / RazorpayX agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Logs and pause help; complete cross-system compensation is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Logs and approvals reduce risk but do not establish guaranteed accuracy or uptime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.5-01.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.5" target="01.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="01.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;01.5.4 · An outage or account lockout leaves me unable to operate&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Keep an incident plan, recovery access and an appropriate fallback channel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Inputs, action logs, permissions, statuses and failure codes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Source freshness, business exceptions, fallback owners and recovery procedures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Require evidence-linked recommendations, action limits and a human fallback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Provider status; device/network health; recovery contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Trading downtime; time to restore essential operations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / RazorpayX agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provider support does not replace an independent operating fallback.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Logs and approvals reduce risk but do not establish guaranteed accuracy or uptime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-01.5-01.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="01.5" target="01.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-02" name="02 Choose the offer and prepare supply">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;02 / Choose the offer and prepare supply&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have the right product, service capacity and economics ready before selling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns assortment, base pricing, supplier readiness, inventory and capacity planning. Executing an accepted order belongs in 06; paying suppliers in 10.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;2A. Assortment and product readiness&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know which products deserve cash, shelf space and attention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Sales economics / inventory capital&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-02.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="02.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.1.1 · I cannot tell whether a bestseller also makes money&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare contribution after product, fulfillment, channel and expected return costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, refunds, processing fees and payment-linked sales trends.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU-level costs, inventory aging, variant catalog, returns and channel fees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join cash outcomes to product costs and suggest stock or assortment reviews.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; SKU sales; landed cost; discounts; shipping; returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Contribution per SKU; loss-making sales.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe / RAY / AP financial inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sales and cost inputs help; full contribution modelling is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment totals cannot identify SKU profit or prove future demand alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.1-02.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.1" target="02.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.1.2 · Slow products trap money that I need for popular products&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Identify aging stock and decide whether to bundle, transfer or stop reordering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, refunds, processing fees and payment-linked sales trends.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU-level costs, inventory aging, variant catalog, returns and channel fees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join cash outcomes to product costs and suggest stock or assortment reviews.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Stock age; sell-through; replenishment lead time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Aged inventory value; working capital released.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — BillMe / RAY / AP financial inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Receipts reveal cash timing; inventory aging needs a separate source.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment totals cannot identify SKU profit or prove future demand alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.1-02.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.1" target="02.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.1.3 · Product variants and descriptions differ across channels&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Maintain accurate, consistent specifications and sellable variants.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, refunds, processing fees and payment-linked sales trends.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU-level costs, inventory aging, variant catalog, returns and channel fees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join cash outcomes to product costs and suggest stock or assortment reviews.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Catalog mismatch; missing attributes; rejected listings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Listing errors; wrong-item orders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — BillMe / RAY / AP financial inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Billing/catalog inputs are adjacent; universal catalog synchronization is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment totals cannot identify SKU profit or prove future demand alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.1-02.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.1" target="02.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.1.4 · I introduce a product without knowing whether demand will repeat&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Test demand with limited exposure and avoid mistaking launch novelty for durable demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, refunds, processing fees and payment-linked sales trends.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU-level costs, inventory aging, variant catalog, returns and channel fees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join cash outcomes to product costs and suggest stock or assortment reviews.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; First/repeat sales; cohorts; waitlist; return reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat demand; unsold launch inventory.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — BillMe / RAY / AP financial inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Aggregate trends are not product-level repeat-demand validation.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment totals cannot identify SKU profit or prove future demand alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.1-02.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.1" target="02.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;2B. Price, bundles and commercial terms&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need prices that customers accept and that leave enough money to run the business.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Pricing / financing / billing terms&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-02.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="02.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.2.1 · My selling price does not reflect rising input costs&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See margin erosion before deciding whether to change price, pack size or supplier.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amounts, discounts, refunds and recurring billing events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product costs, quantities, negotiated terms, service usage and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Model net contribution and make terms or plan changes reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cost changes; margin by SKU; competitor context when permitted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Contribution margin; price-change conversion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Offers / Subscriptions / AP cost inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cost visibility is an input; repricing recommendations are unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 2/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data does not determine willingness to pay or the optimal price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.2-02.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.2" target="02.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.2.2 · A bundle sells well but gives away too much margin&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand bundle economics including component stock and discounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amounts, discounts, refunds and recurring billing events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product costs, quantities, negotiated terms, service usage and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Model net contribution and make terms or plan changes reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Bundle mix; cost allocation; cannibalized standalone sales.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental contribution per bundle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Offers / Subscriptions / AP cost inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Offer tooling exists; optimal bundle economics need external costs.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 2/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data does not determine willingness to pay or the optimal price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.2-02.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.2" target="02.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.2.3 · Wholesale quotes ignore minimum quantities and special handling&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Price order-specific packing, delivery and credit costs explicitly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amounts, discounts, refunds and recurring billing events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product costs, quantities, negotiated terms, service usage and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Model net contribution and make terms or plan changes reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Quote revisions; order size; special requests; payment terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Quote-to-order margin; exceptions per quote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Offers / Subscriptions / AP cost inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supplier-side records help; customer quote costing is separate.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 2/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data does not determine willingness to pay or the optimal price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2541" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.2-02.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.2" target="02.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.2.4 · Subscription plans create billing confusion or unprofitable usage&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Align plan limits, included value and charging terms before selling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amounts, discounts, refunds and recurring billing events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product costs, quantities, negotiated terms, service usage and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Model net contribution and make terms or plan changes reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Usage distribution; plan costs; customer questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Margin by plan; billing complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Offers / Subscriptions / AP cost inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recurring plans are supported; usage economics remain a separate analysis.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data does not determine willingness to pay or the optimal price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3490" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.2-02.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.2" target="02.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;2C. Demand and replenishment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need enough stock for likely demand without betting the business on an optimistic forecast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory financing / reorder decisions&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-02.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="02.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.3.1 · I discover a stockout only after customers try to buy&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Anticipate replenishment using demand, supplier lead time and safety stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Sales receipts, payable commitments and funding availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Stock by SKU/location, lead times, expiry, shrinkage and demand calendar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate cash needed for replenishment and flag financed stock at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Available stock; sales velocity; lead-time variation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Stockout days; unfulfilled demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment / BillMe / AP inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sales inputs help; authoritative stockout prevention is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 1/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financing cannot correct physical counts or create missing demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.3-02.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.3" target="02.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.3.2 · Festival demand makes normal reorder rules unreliable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Use scenarios and uncertainty rather than treating last month as the forecast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Sales receipts, payable commitments and funding availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Stock by SKU/location, lead times, expiry, shrinkage and demand calendar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate cash needed for replenishment and flag financed stock at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Seasonality; campaigns; forecast ranges; stock cover.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Lost peak sales; leftover seasonal stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment / BillMe / AP inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Forecasting revenue is adjacent to festival SKU replenishment.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 2/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financing cannot correct physical counts or create missing demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1570" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.3-02.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.3" target="02.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.3.3 · Online and shop stock are counted separately and oversold&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Maintain available-to-promise stock after reservations and transfers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Sales receipts, payable commitments and funding availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Stock by SKU/location, lead times, expiry, shrinkage and demand calendar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate cash needed for replenishment and flag financed stock at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Stock movements; reservations; sync lag.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Oversell cancellations; stock accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment / BillMe / AP inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cross-location inventory consistency is not established in reviewed products.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 0/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financing cannot correct physical counts or create missing demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2475" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.3-02.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.3" target="02.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.3.4 · Expiry, breakage or shrinkage makes recorded stock misleading&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Distinguish physical, sellable, reserved and damaged units.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Sales receipts, payable commitments and funding availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Stock by SKU/location, lead times, expiry, shrinkage and demand calendar.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate cash needed for replenishment and flag financed stock at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cycle counts; batch expiry; damage logs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Stock write-offs; inventory variance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment / BillMe / AP inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Financial records do not independently detect expiry or shrinkage.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 0/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financing cannot correct physical counts or create missing demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3380" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.3-02.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.3" target="02.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;2D. Suppliers and purchasing readiness&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need reliable supply and a way to recover when a supplier fails.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Procurement / purchase orders / supplier finance&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-02.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="02.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.4.1 · A supplier promises a date but repeatedly delivers late&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track confirmed lead times and prepare alternatives before stock runs out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Approved suppliers, POs, invoices, receipts and payment terms if using AP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Quality inspection, supplier promises, landed costs and alternative quotations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match commercial evidence and compare purchase financing or terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase orders; promised/actual arrival; defect rates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier reliability; stockout exposure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — AP Automation / Source to Pay&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;PO records support monitoring; delivery performance scoring is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 1/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A finance platform cannot ensure the supplier actually delivers acceptable goods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.4-02.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.4" target="02.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.4.2 · The supplier minimum order is larger than I can sell&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare purchase quantity, storage, expiry and cash commitment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Approved suppliers, POs, invoices, receipts and payment terms if using AP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Quality inspection, supplier promises, landed costs and alternative quotations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match commercial evidence and compare purchase financing or terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Minimum quantities; demand forecast; shelf life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Excess purchase value; stock turnover.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — AP Automation / Source to Pay&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;PO controls help; reducing minimum orders or financing all stock is not promised.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 3/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A finance platform cannot ensure the supplier actually delivers acceptable goods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.4-02.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.4" target="02.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.4.3 · The received batch is short or defective and evidence is scattered&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Record receiving checks and resolve quantity/quality differences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Approved suppliers, POs, invoices, receipts and payment terms if using AP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Quality inspection, supplier promises, landed costs and alternative quotations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match commercial evidence and compare purchase financing or terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase order; goods receipt; photos; supplier correspondence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier credit recovered; defect resolution time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — AP Automation / Source to Pay&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Matching improves discrepancy detection; quality evidence still comes from operations.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 1/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A finance platform cannot ensure the supplier actually delivers acceptable goods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2541" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.4-02.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.4" target="02.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.4.4 · I want backup suppliers but cannot compare true landed cost&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare quality, freight, duties, lead time and reliability consistently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Approved suppliers, POs, invoices, receipts and payment terms if using AP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Quality inspection, supplier promises, landed costs and alternative quotations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match commercial evidence and compare purchase financing or terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Quotes; transport; taxes/duties; historical performance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Landed cost; supply concentration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — AP Automation / Source to Pay&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Purchase records help comparisons; complete landed-cost sourcing remains partial.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 2/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A finance platform cannot ensure the supplier actually delivers acceptable goods.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3490" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.4-02.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.4" target="02.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;2E. Service and production capacity&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to sell only the capacity I can reliably deliver.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent:&lt;/b&gt; Capacity economics / wage and asset financing&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-02.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="02.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.5.1 · A service slot appears available but the right employee is not&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Match bookings to skills, calendars and required resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll costs, payment demand by time and capital spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Staff skills, rosters, bookings, machine availability and production dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Quantify the cost of idle capacity or an interruption; support funding decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Staff skills; working hours; room/equipment availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Double bookings; rescheduling rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payroll / payments / capital-adjacent inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payroll records do not determine bookable skills or shifts.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Booking and staff availability connect to service payments.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/5350-create-staff-member-profiles-for-square-appointments&quot;&gt;U07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 0/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Finance can enable capacity but cannot create staff availability or repair machinery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.5-02.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.5" target="02.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.5.2 · Peak demand overwhelms production even though inputs are available&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Plan realistic daily throughput and promise capacity accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll costs, payment demand by time and capital spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Staff skills, rosters, bookings, machine availability and production dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Quantify the cost of idle capacity or an interruption; support funding decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Work-in-progress; task duration; equipment constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Backlog; on-time completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payroll / payments / capital-adjacent inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment peaks are a signal; production scheduling is outside verified scope.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Booking and staff availability connect to service payments.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/5350-create-staff-member-profiles-for-square-appointments&quot;&gt;U07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 0/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Finance can enable capacity but cannot create staff availability or repair machinery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.5-02.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.5" target="02.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.5.3 · Quiet hours waste paid staff time and fixed capacity&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Recognize unused capacity and test suitable offers or schedules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll costs, payment demand by time and capital spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Staff skills, rosters, bookings, machine availability and production dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Quantify the cost of idle capacity or an interruption; support funding decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Utilization by hour; labor availability; demand patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Capacity utilization; contribution per staffed hour.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payroll / payments / capital-adjacent inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cost and receipt data enable analysis; scheduling action is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Booking and staff availability connect to service payments.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/5350-create-staff-member-profiles-for-square-appointments&quot;&gt;U07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 1/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Finance can enable capacity but cannot create staff availability or repair machinery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.5-02.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.5" target="02.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="02.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;02.5.4 · One absent employee or broken machine disrupts every commitment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Create backup capacity and early escalation for critical dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll costs, payment demand by time and capital spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Staff skills, rosters, bookings, machine availability and production dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Quantify the cost of idle capacity or an interruption; support funding decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Single points of failure; absence; maintenance status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Cancelled commitments; recovery time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payroll / payments / capital-adjacent inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Finance can support replacement capacity; interruption prevention remains operational.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Booking and staff availability connect to service payments.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/5350-create-staff-member-profiles-for-square-appointments&quot;&gt;U07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 2/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Finance can enable capacity but cannot create staff availability or repair machinery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-02.5-02.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="02.5" target="02.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-03" name="03 Acquire qualified new demand">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;03 / Acquire qualified new demand&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Help suitable new customers discover and trust the business at an affordable cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns discovery through qualified interest from prospective customers. Checkout friction belongs in 04; campaigns to previous buyers in 09.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;3A. Discovery and channel access&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need a dependable stream of appropriate prospects beyond my existing contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Payment-linked discovery / merchant distribution&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-03.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="03.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.1.1 · People who would value my product never discover the business&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reach a relevant audience through channels the merchant can maintain.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions by channel and identified new customers within the provider footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Audience reach, catalog, location, ad exposure and marketplace conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Identify undersupplied channels and assess acquisition economics with consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Qualified visits; local discovery; inquiry sources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; New qualified prospects; first-order contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / agentic commerce&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Engagement and new commerce channels help; qualified reach is not guaranteed.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/sprint/26&quot;&gt;R20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 1/5 — Affordability-led merchant reach&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Financing options can attract eligible high-value buyers.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A processor does not observe every non-buyer or have automatic cross-merchant marketing rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.1-03.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.1" target="03.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.1.2 · My business depends on one marketplace or advertising platform&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand channel concentration and test affordable alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions by channel and identified new customers within the provider footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Audience reach, catalog, location, ad exposure and marketplace conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Identify undersupplied channels and assess acquisition economics with consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Revenue/lead share by channel; policy interruptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Concentration risk; profitable channel diversity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / agentic commerce&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Multiple payment channels do not eliminate platform dependence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/sprint/26&quot;&gt;R20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 1/5 — Affordability-led merchant reach&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Financing options can attract eligible high-value buyers.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A processor does not observe every non-buyer or have automatic cross-merchant marketing rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.1-03.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.1" target="03.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.1.3 · My offline shop is invisible to nearby people ready to buy&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Keep location, hours, availability and contact information discoverable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions by channel and identified new customers within the provider footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Audience reach, catalog, location, ad exposure and marketplace conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Identify undersupplied channels and assess acquisition economics with consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Local inquiries; inaccurate listings; visit-to-sale records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Qualified footfall; first visits converted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / agentic commerce&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No complete local-intent acquisition workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/sprint/26&quot;&gt;R20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 1/5 — Affordability-led merchant reach&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Financing options can attract eligible high-value buyers.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A processor does not observe every non-buyer or have automatic cross-merchant marketing rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.1-03.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.1" target="03.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.1.4 · My catalog is unsuitable for a new discovery channel&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide accurate structured product information and supported buying paths.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions by channel and identified new customers within the provider footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Audience reach, catalog, location, ad exposure and marketplace conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Identify undersupplied channels and assess acquisition economics with consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Missing attributes; feed errors; rejected products.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Eligible listings; qualified traffic from new channel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / agentic commerce&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Agentic commerce is a channel direction; catalog readiness remains merchant work.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/sprint/26&quot;&gt;R20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 0/5 — Affordability-led merchant reach&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A processor does not observe every non-buyer or have automatic cross-merchant marketing rights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.1-03.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.1" target="03.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;3B. Audience and qualification&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need buyers whose needs fit my offer, not just cheap clicks or a long lead list.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Audience economics / transaction-derived qualification&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-03.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="03.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.2.1 · Ads bring people outside my service area or price range&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Target audiences compatible with delivery, budget and product use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Spend, order value, refunds and repeat transactions for connected identities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Advertising audiences, service area, product fit, inquiries and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare audience contribution and route inquiries using verified business constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Unserviceable leads; location; inquiry reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Qualified lead rate; wasted acquisition spend.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / BillMe segmentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Customer segmentation helps; prospect geography needs campaign data.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment correlation cannot establish a prospect’s intent or eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.2-03.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.2" target="03.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.2.2 · My team spends time on inquiries that will never become orders&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Qualify intent and requirements without dismissing legitimate small buyers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Spend, order value, refunds and repeat transactions for connected identities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Advertising audiences, service area, product fit, inquiries and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare audience contribution and route inquiries using verified business constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Inquiry details; response history; quote acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time per qualified lead; qualification errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe segmentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;General sales-lead qualification is not a verified core workflow.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 0/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment correlation cannot establish a prospect’s intent or eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.2-03.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.2" target="03.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.2.3 · My campaign attracts a use case the product does not actually serve&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Align acquisition promises with verified product suitability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Spend, order value, refunds and repeat transactions for connected identities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Advertising audiences, service area, product fit, inquiries and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare audience contribution and route inquiries using verified business constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Ad claims; inquiry needs; qualification feedback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unsuitable leads; avoidable acquisition spend.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe segmentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Messaging tools do not determine product fit on their own.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 0/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment correlation cannot establish a prospect’s intent or eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.2-03.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.2" target="03.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.2.4 · I cannot tell whether a high-traffic audience is profitable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Evaluate first-order economics and observed later value by acquisition cohort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Spend, order value, refunds and repeat transactions for connected identities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Advertising audiences, service area, product fit, inquiries and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare audience contribution and route inquiries using verified business constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Acquisition source; net sales; returns; contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Acquisition payback; cohort contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / BillMe segmentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Transaction segments help; audience profit needs costs and acquisition data.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 2/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment correlation cannot establish a prospect’s intent or eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.2-03.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.2" target="03.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;3C. Trust and pre-sale questions&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to answer doubts convincingly while protecting the business from promises it cannot keep.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent:&lt;/b&gt; Trust signals / pre-sale financial questions&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-03.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="03.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.3.1 · New shoppers fear the store is unreliable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show clear policies, identity, support access and credible proof.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified merchant account, receipts, complaints, payment and refund policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product facts, delivery promises, reviews, support context and store identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Provide verifiable payment assurances and answer bounded policy questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Trust-related questions; policy visits; checkout exits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Trust-related abandonment; inquiry conversion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Payment identity / Agent Studio / feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognizable payment and refund flows help; business reputation remains separate.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Account verification is not a guarantee of merchant quality or truthful advertising.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.3-03.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.3" target="03.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.3.2 · Prospects ask the same questions but I answer too slowly&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide accurate answers about products, price and service limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified merchant account, receipts, complaints, payment and refund policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product facts, delivery promises, reviews, support context and store identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Provide verifiable payment assurances and answer bounded policy questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Response time; unanswered inquiries; recurring topics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Lead response time; assisted conversion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Payment identity / Agent Studio / feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specialist agents cover defined workflows; broad presales support is partial.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 4/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Account verification is not a guarantee of merchant quality or truthful advertising.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.3-03.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.3" target="03.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.3.3 · An assistant invents a delivery date or product claim to close a sale&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Constrain answers to verified catalog, policies and serviceability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified merchant account, receipts, complaints, payment and refund policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product facts, delivery promises, reviews, support context and store identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Provide verifiable payment assurances and answer bounded policy questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Unsupported answers; promised versus actual service.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Misleading promises; complaint and cancellation rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Payment identity / Agent Studio / feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Guardrails are described; hallucination prevention is not proven.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Account verification is not a guarantee of merchant quality or truthful advertising.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.3-03.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.3" target="03.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.3.4 · Poor or fake reviews distort the first impression of my business&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand legitimate feedback, respond and distinguish suspicious activity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified merchant account, receipts, complaints, payment and refund policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product facts, delivery promises, reviews, support context and store identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Provide verifiable payment assurances and answer bounded policy questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Review patterns; verified orders; recurring concerns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Resolved concerns; trustworthy review coverage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment identity / Agent Studio / feedback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Feedback collection helps; fake-review detection is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/documents-required-for-payment-gateway&quot;&gt;R19&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Account verification is not a guarantee of merchant quality or truthful advertising.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.3-03.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.3" target="03.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;3D. Acquisition spend and creative work&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to learn which investment brings additional profitable customers before scaling it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Marketing spend control / growth finance&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-03.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="03.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.4.1 · I keep spending on ads because revenue rises, despite shrinking profit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare acquired contribution against campaign and fulfillment costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Card/ad spending, receipts, refunds and funding repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Campaign IDs, creative variants, margins, stock and acquisition attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Set affordable campaign budgets and compare contribution before financing expansion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Ad spend; net new orders; discounts; returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; New-customer contribution after acquisition cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards / Engage / RAY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spend controls and campaign data help; causal contribution is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Clearco 1/5 — Ecommerce funding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Funds approved inventory and growth needs.&lt;br&gt;Eligible US ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clear.co/ecommerce-funding&quot;&gt;F28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; More credit or higher sales does not establish positive incremental return.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.4-03.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.4" target="03.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.4.2 · Creative production consumes time with little learning&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Record which messages and product benefits attract suitable customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Card/ad spending, receipts, refunds and funding repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Campaign IDs, creative variants, margins, stock and acquisition attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Set affordable campaign budgets and compare contribution before financing expansion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Creative variants; qualified clicks; first purchases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Cost per useful learning; first-order conversion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Corporate cards / Engage / RAY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Campaign tooling is adjacent; creative learning is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 0/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Clearco 0/5 — Ecommerce funding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;Eligible US ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clear.co/ecommerce-funding&quot;&gt;F28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; More credit or higher sales does not establish positive incremental return.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.4-03.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.4" target="03.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.4.3 · An influencer reports views but I cannot connect them to sales&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Use agreed tracking and realistic attribution limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Card/ad spending, receipts, refunds and funding repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Campaign IDs, creative variants, margins, stock and acquisition attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Set affordable campaign budgets and compare contribution before financing expansion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Links/codes; new customer records; campaign dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Tracked new orders; incremental lift if tested.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards / Engage / RAY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tracked engagement helps; influence attribution remains incomplete.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 1/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Clearco 0/5 — Ecommerce funding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;Eligible US ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clear.co/ecommerce-funding&quot;&gt;F28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; More credit or higher sales does not establish positive incremental return.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.4-03.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.4" target="03.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.4.4 · I scale a campaign just as stock or delivery capacity runs out&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Connect acquisition plans with available supply and fulfillment limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Card/ad spending, receipts, refunds and funding repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Campaign IDs, creative variants, margins, stock and acquisition attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Set affordable campaign budgets and compare contribution before financing expansion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Campaign spend; stock cover; shipping backlog.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Spend on unavailable offers; preventable cancellations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Corporate cards / Engage / RAY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spending controls can pause budgets; stock-aware autonomous scaling is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Clearco 2/5 — Ecommerce funding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Funds approved inventory and growth needs.&lt;br&gt;Eligible US ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clear.co/ecommerce-funding&quot;&gt;F28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; More credit or higher sales does not establish positive incremental return.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3468" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.4-03.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.4" target="03.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;3E. First-customer measurement&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know whether acquisition creates durable demand, without counting the same sale twice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Acquisition measurement / revenue evidence&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-03.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="03.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.5.1 · Several platforms claim credit for the same first purchase&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Use one deduplicated order record and state attribution assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique orders, transaction IDs, refunds and customer identifiers in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Exposure data, channel IDs, cross-channel identity and randomized holdouts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Deduplicate revenue and compare incremental acquired customers with uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order IDs; source claims; attribution windows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate attributed revenue; reporting variance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe / transaction reports&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reports supply outcomes; complete multi-channel attribution is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 2/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment records alone cannot identify why a purchase happened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.5-03.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.5" target="03.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.5.2 · Repeat customers are counted as newly acquired customers&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Resolve identity across store and online channels before calculating acquisition cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique orders, transaction IDs, refunds and customer identifiers in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Exposure data, channel IDs, cross-channel identity and randomized holdouts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Deduplicate revenue and compare incremental acquired customers with uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Customer IDs; matching quality; prior purchase records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Misclassified new customers; acquisition-cost accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Engage / BillMe / transaction reports&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Customer-history segmentation is meaningful within the linked footprint.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 3/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment records alone cannot identify why a purchase happened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.5-03.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.5" target="03.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.5.3 · Campaign results look strong because a festival would have lifted sales anyway&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare against a credible baseline or randomized test when volume permits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique orders, transaction IDs, refunds and customer identifiers in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Exposure data, channel IDs, cross-channel identity and randomized holdouts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Deduplicate revenue and compare incremental acquired customers with uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Holdout/control outcomes; seasonality; confidence intervals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental first orders and contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — Engage / BillMe / transaction reports&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No documented randomized new-customer lift workflow was found.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 0/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment records alone cannot identify why a purchase happened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.5-03.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.5" target="03.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="03.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;03.5.4 · Early campaign data is too small to support a confident decision&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show uncertainty and avoid scaling from a few lucky orders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique orders, transaction IDs, refunds and customer identifiers in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Exposure data, channel IDs, cross-channel identity and randomized holdouts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Deduplicate revenue and compare incremental acquired customers with uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Sample size; variance; conversion lag.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Premature decisions; test completion quality.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe / transaction reports&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Analytics exist; automatic uncertainty-aware decisions are unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment records alone cannot identify why a purchase happened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-03.5-03.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="03.5" target="03.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-04" name="04 Convert intent into an agreed order">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;04 / Convert intent into an agreed order&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Help an interested customer confidently choose and commit to an order, quote or booking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns choice, cart, price disclosure and order commitment. Processing the payment instruction belongs in 05; inventory planning in 02. An abandoned checkout with no attempted payment belongs here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;4A. Choice and order configuration&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need customers to assemble the right order without help or preventable mistakes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent:&lt;/b&gt; Quote / cart / booking connected to payment&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-04.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="04.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.1.1 · Customers cannot select the right size, scent, quantity or service&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Explain options and validate combinations before the order is placed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Quote/payment-link amounts, selected line items and abandoned checkout states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product configuration, service calendar, quote scope and saved cart.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Keep financial terms consistent and support deposits or staged collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Variant changes; help requests; configuration errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Order completion; wrong-variant returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Magic Checkout / Payment Links / Subscriptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout receives selections; product suitability is outside verified scope.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Appointments / Retail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Product and booking configuration integrated with taking payment.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 0/5 — Trade accounts / B2B terms&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment links cannot choose an appropriate product or negotiate commercial scope alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.1-04.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.1" target="04.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.1.2 · A customer wants to change their cart but loses their progress&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Preserve selections and make quantity, address and option edits clear.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Quote/payment-link amounts, selected line items and abandoned checkout states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product configuration, service calendar, quote scope and saved cart.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Keep financial terms consistent and support deposits or staged collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cart edits; session resets; repeated data entry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Edit-to-completion rate; restart frequency.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Magic Checkout / Payment Links / Subscriptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout convenience helps; full cart-edit persistence depends on the store.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Appointments / Retail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Product and booking configuration integrated with taking payment.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 0/5 — Trade accounts / B2B terms&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment links cannot choose an appropriate product or negotiate commercial scope alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.1-04.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.1" target="04.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.1.3 · A complex B2B quote stalls while both sides clarify the scope&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Capture quantities, specifications, delivery and acceptance terms together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Quote/payment-link amounts, selected line items and abandoned checkout states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product configuration, service calendar, quote scope and saved cart.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Keep financial terms consistent and support deposits or staged collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Quote revisions; unanswered questions; scope changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Quote acceptance time; rework after acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Magic Checkout / Payment Links / Subscriptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Collection tools follow an agreement; scope negotiation is not covered.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Appointments / Retail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Product and booking configuration integrated with taking payment.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 2/5 — Trade accounts / B2B terms&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Approved deferred payment terms support B2B ordering.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment links cannot choose an appropriate product or negotiate commercial scope alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.1-04.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.1" target="04.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.1.4 · A service customer cannot find a suitable appointment or package&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show real options and offer a waitlist or alternative time appropriately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Quote/payment-link amounts, selected line items and abandoned checkout states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Product configuration, service calendar, quote scope and saved cart.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Keep financial terms consistent and support deposits or staged collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; No-slot searches; abandoned bookings; waitlist demand.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Booking conversion; unfilled suitable slots.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Magic Checkout / Payment Links / Subscriptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment links collect deposits; an appointment engine is not verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Appointments / Retail&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Product and booking configuration integrated with taking payment.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 0/5 — Trade accounts / B2B terms&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment links cannot choose an appropriate product or negotiate commercial scope alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3468" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.1-04.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.1" target="04.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;4B. Total cost and affordability&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to make the total commitment understandable before the customer loses trust.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout affordability / offers / total-price disclosure&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-04.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="04.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.2.1 · Unexpected shipping or fees make the customer abandon the order&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show payable total and conditions early enough for an informed choice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order total, fees, method eligibility, offers and accepted financed amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping rates, true margins, promotion budgets and customer credit eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain total cost and present eligible payment or offer alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Exits after shipping/tax display; price questions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Cost-surprise abandonment; completed contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / Engage / payment methods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout can show totals; upstream fee choices remain merchant policy.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 1/5 — Affordability / Pay Later&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Partner-led instalments at merchant checkout.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only authorized lenders decide credit; discounts must preserve merchant constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.2-04.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.2" target="04.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.2.2 · A high-value order is unaffordable in one payment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Offer eligible payment options with clear costs and terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order total, fees, method eligibility, offers and accepted financed amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping rates, true margins, promotion budgets and customer credit eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain total cost and present eligible payment or offer alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order value; affordability-option usage; eligibility failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Profitable conversion by payment option.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Magic Checkout / Engage / payment methods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Affordability options address eligible buyers, not universal purchasing power.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 4/5 — Affordability / Pay Later&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Partner-led instalments at merchant checkout.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only authorized lenders decide credit; discounts must preserve merchant constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.2-04.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.2" target="04.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.2.3 · Coupon conditions are confusing or the code does not work&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Explain eligibility and apply permitted offers consistently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order total, fees, method eligibility, offers and accepted financed amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping rates, true margins, promotion budgets and customer credit eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain total cost and present eligible payment or offer alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Coupon errors; stacking attempts; support contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Offer redemption errors; checkout completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / Engage / payment methods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Offer presentation helps; rules and integration must match actual eligibility.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 3/5 — Affordability / Pay Later&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Partner-led instalments at merchant checkout.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only authorized lenders decide credit; discounts must preserve merchant constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.2-04.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.2" target="04.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.2.4 · A discount increases orders but makes the order unprofitable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Set contribution-aware limits before exposing an offer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order total, fees, method eligibility, offers and accepted financed amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping rates, true margins, promotion budgets and customer credit eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Explain total cost and present eligible payment or offer alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cart costs; discount combinations; shipping subsidy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Contribution per completed order; below-floor orders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Magic Checkout / Engage / payment methods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Offer tools do not independently guarantee order contribution.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pine Labs 1/5 — Affordability / Pay Later&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Partner-led instalments at merchant checkout.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinelabs.com/pos-products/paylater&quot;&gt;F30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only authorized lenders decide credit; discounts must preserve merchant constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3468" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.2-04.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.2" target="04.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;4C. Checkout usability and accessibility&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need a short, reliable buying path for the devices and languages my customers actually use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Hosted checkout / tokenization / POS&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-04.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="04.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.3.1 · Customers repeatedly type details on a small mobile screen&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reduce unnecessary entry and validate clearly without losing information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Session errors, completion time, chosen method and payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Device accessibility, page speed, store queue and customer input behavior.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Remove redundant entry, surface checkout defects and simplify acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Field errors; completion time; device/browser breakdown.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout completion; field abandonment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Magic Checkout / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prefill and checkout convenience directly address repeated entry.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The merchant site, network and physical staffing still influence completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.3-04.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.3" target="04.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.3.2 · Forced signup blocks a customer who only wants to buy once&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Allow an appropriate low-friction path and explain any necessary account step.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Session errors, completion time, chosen method and payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Device accessibility, page speed, store queue and customer input behavior.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Remove redundant entry, surface checkout defects and simplify acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Signup exits; authentication errors; guest completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Account-step abandonment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A simpler checkout helps; mandatory store signup is still merchant-controlled.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The merchant site, network and physical staffing still influence completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.3-04.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.3" target="04.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.3.3 · The checkout is slow, broken or hard to understand&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Identify actual friction by device, accessibility needs and language.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Session errors, completion time, chosen method and payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Device accessibility, page speed, store queue and customer input behavior.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Remove redundant entry, surface checkout defects and simplify acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Load time; error logs; session events; usability observations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Completion by device/language; critical errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hosted payment UX covers part of the site performance problem.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The merchant site, network and physical staffing still influence completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.3-04.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.3" target="04.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.3.4 · Store queues make in-person customers leave before billing&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Speed item entry and support suitable queue/payment arrangements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Session errors, completion time, chosen method and payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Device accessibility, page speed, store queue and customer input behavior.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Remove redundant entry, surface checkout defects and simplify acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Queue time; billing duration; abandoned queues.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Served customers per hour; queue abandonment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;POS directly helps acceptance; queues also depend on staffing and billing.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 1/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; The merchant site, network and physical staffing still influence completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.3-04.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.3" target="04.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;4D. Promise and confidence before commitment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need the customer to understand what they will receive and when.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Order promise / COD risk / confirmation&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-04.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="04.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.4.1 · The delivery promise is unclear until after purchase&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show realistic dates and location restrictions before commitment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order totals, payment state, COD/prepaid choice and risk inputs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Serviceable address, delivery capacity, return policy and booking acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate financial commitment and offer approved alternatives when risk is high.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Serviceability; carrier estimates; date-related exits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Promise-related abandonment; late commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Magic Checkout / Agent Studio COD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout can expose a promise; fulfillment accuracy needs logistics data.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — Connected engagement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-context messaging and engagement.&lt;br&gt;India / ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A risk score should not be mistaken for proof of customer intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.4-04.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.4" target="04.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.4.2 · The customer cannot find return or cancellation conditions&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make applicable policies visible and understandable at decision time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order totals, payment state, COD/prepaid choice and risk inputs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Serviceable address, delivery capacity, return policy and booking acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate financial commitment and offer approved alternatives when risk is high.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Policy searches; support questions; policy-page exits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Policy-related abandonment; later misunderstandings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Magic Checkout / Agent Studio COD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Policies can be presented; correctness remains merchant-owned.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — Connected engagement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-context messaging and engagement.&lt;br&gt;India / ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A risk score should not be mistaken for proof of customer intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1570" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.4-04.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.4" target="04.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.4.3 · COD choice attracts orders that may never be accepted&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Balance buyer preference with explainable risk and prepaid alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order totals, payment state, COD/prepaid choice and risk inputs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Serviceable address, delivery capacity, return policy and booking acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate financial commitment and offer approved alternatives when risk is high.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; COD acceptance; customer history; location/order risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Delivered contribution; legitimate buyers blocked.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / Agent Studio COD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;COD confirmation and risk tools overlap directly; false blocks remain possible.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — Connected engagement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-context messaging and engagement.&lt;br&gt;India / ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A risk score should not be mistaken for proof of customer intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2475" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.4-04.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.4" target="04.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.4.4 · The customer is unsure whether the order or booking was accepted&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show an unambiguous confirmation and route unresolved status checks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Order totals, payment state, COD/prepaid choice and risk inputs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Serviceable address, delivery capacity, return policy and booking acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate financial commitment and offer approved alternatives when risk is high.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Missing confirmation; duplicate submissions; status inquiries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate orders; confirmation-related contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / Agent Studio COD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment/order status helps; confirmation requires correct system integration.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 3/5 — Connected engagement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Order-context messaging and engagement.&lt;br&gt;India / ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A risk score should not be mistaken for proof of customer intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3380" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.4-04.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.4" target="04.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;4E. Abandoned-intent recovery&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to recover genuine unfinished purchases without chasing people who were only browsing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Abandoned-intent messaging / payment links&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-04.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="04.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.5.1 · I treat every abandoned cart as money that can be recovered&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Separate browsing, price comparison, technical friction and genuine intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout or cart events only when integrated; subsequent payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent, current cart, purchase across channels, product margins and suppression lists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Rank recoverable intent and coordinate permitted reminders or offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Abandonment stage; payment attempts; customer response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Recovery eligibility accuracy; wasted contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio cart recovery / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recovery agent exists; realizable value and incremental lift need validation.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Marketing automation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connected customer and engagement workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A cart total is an opportunity estimate, not earned or certainly recoverable revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.5-04.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.5" target="04.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.5.2 · Recovery messages arrive after the customer already purchased&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Check current order state and stop redundant follow-ups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout or cart events only when integrated; subsequent payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent, current cart, purchase across channels, product margins and suppression lists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Rank recoverable intent and coordinate permitted reminders or offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Latest order status; message queue delay; cross-device match.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Messages after purchase; complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Agent Studio cart recovery / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Context-aware actions help; purchases outside connected sources may be missed.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 3/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Marketing automation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connected customer and engagement workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A cart total is an opportunity estimate, not earned or certainly recoverable revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.5-04.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.5" target="04.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.5.3 · Every recovery attempt starts with a discount&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Address the actual objection using approved options, including no incentive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout or cart events only when integrated; subsequent payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent, current cart, purchase across channels, product margins and suppression lists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Rank recoverable intent and coordinate permitted reminders or offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Reason for abandonment; offer history; contribution floor.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental recovered contribution; discount leakage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Agent Studio cart recovery / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Approved-offer controls help avoid arbitrary discounts.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 3/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Marketing automation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connected customer and engagement workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A cart total is an opportunity estimate, not earned or certainly recoverable revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.5-04.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.5" target="04.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="04.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;04.5.4 · Several tools contact the same person repeatedly&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Coordinate contact timing, consent, frequency and stopping conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Checkout or cart events only when integrated; subsequent payment outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Consent, current cart, purchase across channels, product margins and suppression lists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Rank recoverable intent and coordinate permitted reminders or offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cross-tool contact history; opt-out; purchase completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate outreach; net recovery after contact costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio cart recovery / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;One workflow can enforce limits; cross-vendor orchestration is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Marketing automation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connected customer and engagement workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A cart total is an opportunity estimate, not earned or certainly recoverable revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3468" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-04.5-04.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="04.5" target="04.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-05" name="05 Collect the agreed customer payment">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;05 / Collect the agreed customer payment&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turn an authorized amount due into one verified successful collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns payment authorization, failures, recurring debits and overdue invoices. Funds already collected but not received/matched belong in 08. Voluntary relationship churn belongs in 09.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;5A. Authorization and payment success&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need willing customers to complete payment through a working method.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Payment acceptance / routing / authentication&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-05.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="05.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.1.1 · A bank or payment route fails even though the buyer wants to pay&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Identify the failing route and offer a supported alternative safely.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Attempt status, method, issuer/route, failure codes and timestamps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Order intent, supported fallback options and merchant-country configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Diagnose the failed route and present a safe supported alternative.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Failure codes; issuer/method/time success; provider health.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Payment success rate; unique orders recovered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Optimizer / payment gateway / international collections&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Routing directly addresses route-level failure within supported providers.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/optimizer-intelligent-payments-routing/&quot;&gt;R11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 4/5 — FlowWise payment routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment route orchestration to respond to performance conditions.&lt;br&gt;India / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/blog/smart-payment-routing/&quot;&gt;I01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; No processor controls every issuer or can guarantee all legitimate payments succeed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.1-05.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.1" target="05.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.1.2 · The preferred payment method is missing or ineligible&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Explain supported methods and offer relevant available alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Attempt status, method, issuer/route, failure codes and timestamps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Order intent, supported fallback options and merchant-country configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Diagnose the failed route and present a safe supported alternative.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Method selection; eligibility failures; method-related exits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Payment completion by method and customer group.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Optimizer / payment gateway / international collections&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Broad methods help; bank, device and buyer eligibility still apply.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/optimizer-intelligent-payments-routing/&quot;&gt;R11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 3/5 — FlowWise payment routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment route orchestration to respond to performance conditions.&lt;br&gt;India / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/blog/smart-payment-routing/&quot;&gt;I01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; No processor controls every issuer or can guarantee all legitimate payments succeed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.1-05.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.1" target="05.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.1.3 · Authentication times out or an app switch breaks the journey&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Preserve payment context and clearly explain recovery steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Attempt status, method, issuer/route, failure codes and timestamps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Order intent, supported fallback options and merchant-country configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Diagnose the failed route and present a safe supported alternative.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; OTP/3DS/app-switch events; timeouts; return callbacks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Authentication completion; retries per order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Optimizer / payment gateway / international collections&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Optimized payment flows help; external authentication remains a constraint.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/optimizer-intelligent-payments-routing/&quot;&gt;R11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 3/5 — FlowWise payment routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment route orchestration to respond to performance conditions.&lt;br&gt;India / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/blog/smart-payment-routing/&quot;&gt;I01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; No processor controls every issuer or can guarantee all legitimate payments succeed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.1-05.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.1" target="05.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.1.4 · International customers cannot pay with familiar local options&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Offer supported currencies, methods and authentication flows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Attempt status, method, issuer/route, failure codes and timestamps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Order intent, supported fallback options and merchant-country configuration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Diagnose the failed route and present a safe supported alternative.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Country/issuer declines; method coverage; FX presentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Cross-border authorization and completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Optimizer / payment gateway / international collections&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;International acceptance exists; familiar local methods vary by market.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/optimizer-intelligent-payments-routing/&quot;&gt;R11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/solutions/e-commerce/&quot;&gt;F44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 2/5 — FlowWise payment routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment route orchestration to respond to performance conditions.&lt;br&gt;India / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/blog/smart-payment-routing/&quot;&gt;I01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; No processor controls every issuer or can guarantee all legitimate payments succeed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.1-05.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.1" target="05.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;5B. Ambiguous and duplicate collections&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need one trustworthy answer about whether money was collected before acting again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Collection status / capture / reconciliation&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-05.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="05.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.2.1 · The customer says money was debited but my order shows unpaid&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Check the authoritative payment state and explain pending resolution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment ID, order reference, authorization, capture and refund events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Merchant order state, cashier confirmation and customer claim.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recheck authoritative status, prevent duplicate actions and escalate stale states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/order IDs; pending status; bank/provider events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Resolution time; duplicate payment requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Payments dashboard / order integration / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment-state lookup and reconciliation support ambiguous outcomes.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — POS transaction records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. In-person payment state and order-linked records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A screenshot or webhook arrival alone should not overrule authoritative records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.2-05.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.2" target="05.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.2.2 · A retry collects twice for the same purchase&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Tie retries to the same obligation and prevent duplicate collection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment ID, order reference, authorization, capture and refund events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Merchant order state, cashier confirmation and customer claim.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recheck authoritative status, prevent duplicate actions and escalate stale states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate references; amounts; timestamps; retry requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate charges per unique order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Payments dashboard / order integration / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Safe integration can prevent duplicates; incorrect external retries remain possible.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — POS transaction records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. In-person payment state and order-linked records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A screenshot or webhook arrival alone should not overrule authoritative records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.2-05.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.2" target="05.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.2.3 · A card payment is authorized but never captured&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track authorization expiry and capture according to the order workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment ID, order reference, authorization, capture and refund events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Merchant order state, cashier confirmation and customer claim.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recheck authoritative status, prevent duplicate actions and escalate stale states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Authorized-not-captured age; capture failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Expired authorizations; recoverable capture value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Payments dashboard / order integration / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Capture workflow is supported; timeout monitoring still matters.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — POS transaction records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. In-person payment state and order-linked records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A screenshot or webhook arrival alone should not overrule authoritative records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.2-05.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.2" target="05.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.2.4 · A cashier accepts a payment screenshot as proof&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Verify the actual received transaction before marking the bill paid.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment ID, order reference, authorization, capture and refund events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Merchant order state, cashier confirmation and customer claim.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Recheck authoritative status, prevent duplicate actions and escalate stale states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Provider confirmation; receipt/reference match.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; False payment acknowledgments; cash loss.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Payments dashboard / order integration / POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;POS confirmation reduces screenshot dependence; staff must use verified status.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/pos/&quot;&gt;F07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — POS transaction records&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. In-person payment state and order-linked records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A screenshot or webhook arrival alone should not overrule authoritative records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.2-05.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.2" target="05.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;5C. Recurring payment execution&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need consented recurring payments to run reliably while respecting customer changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Mandates / subscription billing / retry&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-05.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="05.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.3.1 · A subscriber abandons mandate setup before the first debit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Explain the mandate and resume incomplete registration appropriately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Mandate state, debit schedule, failure codes and renewal/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer entitlement, changed plans, alternate payments and contact preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Fix setup friction, time permitted retries and keep billing synchronized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Setup stage; authorization status; consent record.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Mandate completion; first successful debit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Subscriptions / UPI AutoPay / revenue recovery agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mandate setup is supported; abandonment cannot be eliminated.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Canceling service, canceling a mandate and recording a payment must be reconciled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.3-05.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.3" target="05.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.3.2 · A renewal fails because funds or the payment instrument are temporarily unavailable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Choose permitted retry timing and an alternate recovery path.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Mandate state, debit schedule, failure codes and renewal/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer entitlement, changed plans, alternate payments and contact preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Fix setup friction, time permitted retries and keep billing synchronized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Failure reason; mandate/card state; retry outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Recovered renewals; avoidable service interruption.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Subscriptions / UPI AutoPay / revenue recovery agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Retry and recovery tools exist; AutoPay feature rollout may be limited.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Canceling service, canceling a mandate and recording a payment must be reconciled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1614" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.3-05.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.3" target="05.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.3.3 · Retries keep running after a customer cancels or pays another way&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Synchronize entitlement, mandate and outstanding-balance state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Mandate state, debit schedule, failure codes and renewal/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer entitlement, changed plans, alternate payments and contact preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Fix setup friction, time permitted retries and keep billing synchronized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cancellation time; latest payment; queued retries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Charges after cancellation; redundant retry cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Subscriptions / UPI AutoPay / revenue recovery agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cancellation/state events help; external-payment joins remain necessary.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Canceling service, canceling a mandate and recording a payment must be reconciled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2585" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.3-05.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.3" target="05.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.3.4 · Plan changes create the wrong amount or billing date&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile agreed plan terms, proration and billing schedule before charging.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Mandate state, debit schedule, failure codes and renewal/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer entitlement, changed plans, alternate payments and contact preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Fix setup friction, time permitted retries and keep billing synchronized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Plan events; amount changes; billing calculations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Billing errors; credit adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Subscriptions / UPI AutoPay / revenue recovery agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Plan lifecycle tooling exists; supported methods and change rules differ.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Canceling service, canceling a mandate and recording a payment must be reconciled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3556" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.3-05.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.3" target="05.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;5D. Invoices and trade credit collection&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to get paid on time without damaging a useful customer relationship.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Accounts receivable / invoice collection / trade credit&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-05.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="05.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.4.1 · I forget which business customers owe me and when&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Maintain an accurate aging view with one owner for each follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice amount/due date, payment reference, part-payment and aging if integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Debtor contacts, disputes, promised payments and approved credit policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize overdue balances, reconcile deductions and prepare contextual reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice due date; open balance; aging buckets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Days sales outstanding; overdue balance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Smart Collect / invoices / receivables agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Invoice and collection views help; agent availability needs confirmation.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 4/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 3/5 — B2B trade accounts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Approved trade accounts and deferred collections.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Collecting a debt is different from approving more credit or resolving a contract dispute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.4-05.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.4" target="05.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.4.2 · A reminder goes to the wrong contact or ignores a payment dispute&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Contact the responsible person with the invoice context and pause unresolved cases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice amount/due date, payment reference, part-payment and aging if integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Debtor contacts, disputes, promised payments and approved credit policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize overdue balances, reconcile deductions and prepare contextual reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Accounts-payable contact; dispute notes; reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Reminder relevance; time to resolution/payment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Smart Collect / invoices / receivables agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Contextual receivables assistance is described; dispute-aware suppression needs testing.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 2/5 — B2B trade accounts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Approved trade accounts and deferred collections.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Collecting a debt is different from approving more credit or resolving a contract dispute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.4-05.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.4" target="05.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.4.3 · A customer makes a part-payment without explaining the deduction&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track the remaining obligation and distinguish deduction from settlement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice amount/due date, payment reference, part-payment and aging if integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Debtor contacts, disputes, promised payments and approved credit policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize overdue balances, reconcile deductions and prepare contextual reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice balance; remittance details; credits; withholding.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unresolved deductions; collection accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Smart Collect / invoices / receivables agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;References and receipt matching help; short-pay reasoning remains partial.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 3/5 — B2B trade accounts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Approved trade accounts and deferred collections.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Collecting a debt is different from approving more credit or resolving a contract dispute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2541" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.4-05.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.4" target="05.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.4.4 · Late-paying customers keep placing new orders on credit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make credit exposure visible before extending more terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice amount/due date, payment reference, part-payment and aging if integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Debtor contacts, disputes, promised payments and approved credit policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize overdue balances, reconcile deductions and prepare contextual reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Overdue balance; open orders; agreed credit limit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Bad debt exposure; overdue concentration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Smart Collect / invoices / receivables agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No general merchant trade-credit policy engine was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 2/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mondu 4/5 — B2B trade accounts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Approved trade accounts and deferred collections.&lt;br&gt;UK / Europe · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mondu.ai/en-gb/partnerships/&quot;&gt;F27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Collecting a debt is different from approving more credit or resolving a contract dispute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3490" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.4-05.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.4" target="05.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;5E. Recovery economics and customer treatment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need recovery effort to be proportionate, permitted and measurable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Recovery operations / fair treatment / value measurement&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-05.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="05.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.5.1 · I cannot prioritize which failed payments or invoices to work first&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Rank by recoverable value, age, reason, cost and customer context.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Failed obligations, retry history, collection fees and unique successful payments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Contact permissions, disputes, expected recovery, costs and treatment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Choose a permitted next step and compare net unique recoveries with a baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Unique unpaid obligations; reason; contact cost; probability estimates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Net cash recovered per unit of effort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / AutoPay recovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recovery tools provide workflows; optimal cross-product prioritization is not proven.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Repeated attempts are not additional sales; contact and repayment constraints apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.5-05.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.5" target="05.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.5.2 · Repeated retries or calls cost more than the amount recovered&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Limit attempts and stop when expected recovery no longer justifies cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Failed obligations, retry history, collection fees and unique successful payments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Contact permissions, disputes, expected recovery, costs and treatment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Choose a permitted next step and compare net unique recoveries with a baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Attempt count; provider/message fees; response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Recovery contribution after fees; wasted attempts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / AutoPay recovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Automation reduces effort; cost-aware stopping is not fully established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 2/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Repeated attempts are not additional sales; contact and repayment constraints apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1636" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.5-05.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.5" target="05.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.5.3 · Someone already rejected further contact but the recovery flow continues&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Honor consent, refusal and approved channel/frequency limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Failed obligations, retry history, collection fees and unique successful payments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Contact permissions, disputes, expected recovery, costs and treatment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Choose a permitted next step and compare net unique recoveries with a baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Opt-out; call outcome; suppression state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Prohibited contacts; complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / AutoPay recovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Consent checks are described; all external opt-outs must be joined.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 2/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Repeated attempts are not additional sales; contact and repayment constraints apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2607" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.5-05.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.5" target="05.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="05.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;05.5.4 · Recovered-payment reports count retries as separate sales&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Measure distinct paid obligations and account for later refunds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Failed obligations, retry history, collection fees and unique successful payments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Contact permissions, disputes, expected recovery, costs and treatment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Choose a permitted next step and compare net unique recoveries with a baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order/invoice IDs; attempts; refunds; recovery attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Deduplicated net recovery; reporting accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Agent Studio / RAY / AutoPay recovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Transaction reporting helps deduplication; causal recovery still needs a baseline.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/?p=26313&quot;&gt;R12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Repeated attempts are not additional sales; contact and repayment constraints apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3578" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-05.5-05.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="05.5" target="05.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-06" name="06 Deliver the promised value">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;06 / Deliver the promised value&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Complete each accepted order or service reliably, at a sustainable cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns order execution, dispatch, delivery, service delivery and failed-delivery/RTO prevention. Post-delivery returns or compensation belong in 07; stock planning in 02; carrier COD remittance in 08.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;6A. Order handoff and preparation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need every accepted order to become an accurate task that someone owns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Paid-order handoff / fulfillment release&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-06.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="06.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.1.1 · A paid order never reaches the packing team&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Detect missing handoffs between order capture and fulfillment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified paid/captured status and refund/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Packing queue, SKUs, stock reservation, address changes and dispatch state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Release only valid orders, flag missing handoffs and show revenue at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Paid orders without fulfillment task; event delay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Orders stuck before preparation; handoff time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Payment webhooks / Magic Checkout integration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment events enable handoff; the store must consume and act on them.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial confirmation cannot guarantee correct picking or physical execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.1-06.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.1" target="06.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.1.2 · Workers pick the wrong variant or omit an item&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Match picking and packing to the accepted order and record checks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified paid/captured status and refund/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Packing queue, SKUs, stock reservation, address changes and dispatch state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Release only valid orders, flag missing handoffs and show revenue at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Pick scans; packing checks; mismatch reports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Wrong/missing-item rate; rework cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — Payment webhooks / Magic Checkout integration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct packing-accuracy workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 0/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial confirmation cannot guarantee correct picking or physical execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1592" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.1-06.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.1" target="06.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.1.3 · Urgent and ordinary orders compete with no clear priority&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Sequence work by commitment, availability and delivery cutoff.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified paid/captured status and refund/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Packing queue, SKUs, stock reservation, address changes and dispatch state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Release only valid orders, flag missing handoffs and show revenue at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Promised dates; queue age; cutoff; order readiness.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; On-time dispatch; urgent-order misses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment webhooks / Magic Checkout integration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment value is an input; packing priority needs operational rules.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 1/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial confirmation cannot guarantee correct picking or physical execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2497" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.1-06.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.1" target="06.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.1.4 · A customer changes an address or item after preparation starts&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Apply changes only while feasible and synchronize every affected system.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Verified paid/captured status and refund/cancellation events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Packing queue, SKUs, stock reservation, address changes and dispatch state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Release only valid orders, flag missing handoffs and show revenue at risk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order stage; edit timestamps; label/packing state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Avoidable reshipments; change handling time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment webhooks / Magic Checkout integration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout data helps at order time; post-packing changes need the fulfillment tool.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 1/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial confirmation cannot guarantee correct picking or physical execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3424" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.1-06.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.1" target="06.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;6B. Dispatch and carrier choice&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need the delivery option that best fits the promised service and order economics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent:&lt;/b&gt; Logistics economics / carrier invoices / transit protection&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-06.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="06.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.2.1 · The cheapest courier performs poorly on particular routes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare route-level reliability, price and promise fit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping bills and paid order value where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Lane reliability, pickup events, dimensions, parcel splits and claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare delivered contribution after freight and flag unsupported charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier/pincode delivery rate; delay; total shipping cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Delivered contribution; on-time delivery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — AP / financial records; no core carrier planner&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Financial cost data helps; route-level courier optimization is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 4/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier selection and physical service remain operational; fintech supplies costs or protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.2-06.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.2" target="06.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.2.2 · Missed pickups cause late delivery despite on-time packing&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track pickup commitments and escalate before the cutoff is lost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping bills and paid order value where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Lane reliability, pickup events, dimensions, parcel splits and claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare delivered contribution after freight and flag unsupported charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Ready time; pickup scans; failed pickup records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Pickup adherence; dispatch delay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — AP / financial records; no core carrier planner&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct pickup execution workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 1/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier selection and physical service remain operational; fintech supplies costs or protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.2-06.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.2" target="06.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.2.3 · Packaging dimensions cause unexpected shipping charges&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Record accurate package measurements and audit billed differences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping bills and paid order value where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Lane reliability, pickup events, dimensions, parcel splits and claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare delivered contribution after freight and flag unsupported charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Measured/billed weight; dimensions; packaging type.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping variance; disputed charges recovered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — AP / financial records; no core carrier planner&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AP records expose charges; weight disputes need shipment evidence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier selection and physical service remain operational; fintech supplies costs or protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.2-06.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.2" target="06.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.2.4 · Multi-package or split orders confuse customers and staff&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track each parcel against one order and explain separate arrivals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Shipping bills and paid order value where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Lane reliability, pickup events, dimensions, parcel splits and claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare delivered contribution after freight and flag unsupported charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Parcel IDs; item allocation; delivery status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Split-order inquiries; missing-parcel incidents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — AP / financial records; no core carrier planner&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment data does not manage split-parcel communication.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Carrier selection and physical service remain operational; fintech supplies costs or protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.2-06.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.2" target="06.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;6C. In-transit visibility and intervention&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to fix delivery problems while a sale can still be saved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent:&lt;/b&gt; In-transit financial risk / cross-border documents&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-06.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="06.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.3.1 · Customers keep asking where their order is&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide current tracking and proactively explain meaningful delays.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amount, refunds and insurance/finance exposure where contracted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Tracking scans, delivery exceptions, customs documents and support messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Surface value at risk and prepare evidence for permitted logistics intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Tracking freshness; delay events; contact reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Where-is-my-order contacts; resolution time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment context / support integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Order/payment context helps support; native tracking is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 4/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 4/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Processor records alone cannot locate a parcel or release customs holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.3-06.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.3" target="06.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.3.2 · The courier marks a customer unreachable without a useful next step&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm the issue and request a feasible reattempt promptly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amount, refunds and insurance/finance exposure where contracted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Tracking scans, delivery exceptions, customs documents and support messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Surface value at risk and prepare evidence for permitted logistics intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; NDR reason; customer response; reattempt window.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; NDR recovery; avoidable RTO.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment context / support integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specialist context is adjacent; courier follow-up is a logistics workflow.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 4/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 3/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Processor records alone cannot locate a parcel or release customs holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.3-06.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.3" target="06.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.3.3 · A parcel is stuck but nobody notices until the customer complains&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Flag abnormal transit and assign follow-up ownership.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amount, refunds and insurance/finance exposure where contracted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Tracking scans, delivery exceptions, customs documents and support messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Surface value at risk and prepare evidence for permitted logistics intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Time since scan; route benchmark; carrier exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to detect/resolve delay; late deliveries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment context / support integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Financial exposure can prioritize cases; tracking requires external events.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 3/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Processor records alone cannot locate a parcel or release customs holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.3-06.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.3" target="06.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.3.4 · An international shipment stalls over missing information&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare required shipment data and coordinate exception resolution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid amount, refunds and insurance/finance exposure where contracted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Tracking scans, delivery exceptions, customs documents and support messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Surface value at risk and prepare evidence for permitted logistics intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Customs holds; missing invoice fields; carrier requests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Clearance time; avoidable international cancellations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Payment context / support integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment records assist documentation; customs execution is outside verified scope.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 2/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Processor records alone cannot locate a parcel or release customs holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent operational need&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.3-06.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.3" target="06.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;6D. Acceptance and failed-delivery prevention&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need legitimate orders to be accepted without rejecting good customers unnecessarily.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; COD risk / address validation / RTO economics&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-06.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="06.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.4.1 · COD buyers forget or change their minds before delivery&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm intent and communicate the actual delivery/payment expectations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment choice, prepaid conversion and connected historical outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Address serviceability, delivery confirmation, COD acceptance and returned stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm intent, offer eligible alternatives and monitor loss versus false rejection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Confirmation response; delivery date; acceptance history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; COD acceptance; net delivered contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / COD agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;COD confirmation targets this problem; acceptance cannot be guaranteed.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 3/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Past outcomes do not prove current intent; errors need review and correction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.4-06.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.4" target="06.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.4.2 · A delivery address is incomplete or unserviceable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Correct necessary details before dispatch or a reattempt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment choice, prepaid conversion and connected historical outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Address serviceability, delivery confirmation, COD acceptance and returned stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm intent, offer eligible alternatives and monitor loss versus false rejection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Address errors; serviceability; delivery feedback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Address-caused delivery failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Magic Checkout / COD agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checkout address tools help; carrier serviceability must remain current.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Past outcomes do not prove current intent; errors need review and correction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.4-06.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.4" target="06.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.4.3 · Risk rules block too many genuine COD customers&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Review error rates and allow appropriate approved alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment choice, prepaid conversion and connected historical outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Address serviceability, delivery confirmation, COD acceptance and returned stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm intent, offer eligible alternatives and monitor loss versus false rejection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Blocked orders; successful appeals; later outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; False blocks; losses avoided versus sales lost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Magic Checkout / COD agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Risk decisions need error-rate visibility; fair-review coverage is not fully verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 2/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 2/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Past outcomes do not prove current intent; errors need review and correction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.4-06.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.4" target="06.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.4.4 · Returned-to-origin parcels disappear from sellable stock for weeks&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track reverse transit, receiving and condition before restocking.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment choice, prepaid conversion and connected historical outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Address serviceability, delivery confirmation, COD acceptance and returned stock.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm intent, offer eligible alternatives and monitor loss versus false rejection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; RTO status; inbound scan; condition check.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; RTO cycle time; inventory recovered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Magic Checkout / COD agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;RTO prevention helps upstream; returned-stock control remains external.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Shiprocket 3/5 — Shipping / NDR&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Shipping and failed-delivery workflows with transaction consequences.&lt;br&gt;India / supported routes · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shiprocket.in/features/&quot;&gt;I04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://support.shiprocket.in/support/solutions/folders/152000000132&quot;&gt;I05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;GoKwik 1/5 — KwikEngage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Messaging and engagement linked to merchant customer and order context.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gokwik.co/product/kwikengage&quot;&gt;I03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Past outcomes do not prove current intent; errors need review and correction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.4-06.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.4" target="06.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;6E. Service and digital delivery&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need customers to receive the booked service or digital entitlement at the promised time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Deposits / entitlements / milestone evidence&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-06.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="06.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.5.1 · A customer does not show up and the reserved slot is wasted&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Confirm appointments, offer rescheduling and apply disclosed policies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/deposit status, subscription entitlement trigger and invoice reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, service schedule, access provisioning and signed acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Connect valid payment to delivery, enforce approved deposit policy and preserve evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance; reminder response; cancellation time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; No-show rate; recovered capacity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Payment Links / Subscriptions / events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deposits help deter no-shows; full attendance management is external.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Booking, payment and no-show-related workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 1/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment is not proof of attendance, useful service or accepted work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.5-06.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.5" target="06.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.5.2 · Staff delays cascade into every later appointment&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Detect schedule slippage and coordinate realistic customer updates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/deposit status, subscription entitlement trigger and invoice reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, service schedule, access provisioning and signed acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Connect valid payment to delivery, enforce approved deposit policy and preserve evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Actual service duration; queue; staff status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Wait time; late starts; rescheduling cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — Payment Links / Subscriptions / events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No service-scheduling engine was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Booking, payment and no-show-related workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 0/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct support found fit for this specific pain. The cited offering addresses a neighboring job rather than this need.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment is not proof of attendance, useful service or accepted work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1592" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.5-06.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.5" target="06.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.5.3 · Payment succeeds but digital access is never granted&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Connect verified payment with correct entitlement and repair failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/deposit status, subscription entitlement trigger and invoice reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, service schedule, access provisioning and signed acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Connect valid payment to delivery, enforce approved deposit policy and preserve evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/entitlement mismatch; provisioning errors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to access; paid-but-blocked customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Payment Links / Subscriptions / events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Subscription/payment events support provisioning; the app must grant access.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Booking, payment and no-show-related workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment is not proof of attendance, useful service or accepted work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2497" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.5-06.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.5" target="06.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="06.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;06.5.4 · B2B work is delivered but acceptance proof is missing&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Capture agreed milestones, delivery records and customer acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment/deposit status, subscription entitlement trigger and invoice reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, service schedule, access provisioning and signed acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Connect valid payment to delivery, enforce approved deposit policy and preserve evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Work completion; sign-off; delivery evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unaccepted completed work; billing delay.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Payment Links / Subscriptions / events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Invoices record a claim; signed delivery acceptance needs a separate source.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/payment-gateway/web-integration/standard/integration-steps/&quot;&gt;R17&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Appointments&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Booking, payment and no-show-related workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/appointments&quot;&gt;U06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Payments / Billing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment lifecycle, integration events and recurring collection tools.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents&quot;&gt;F09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks&quot;&gt;F10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/how-we-built-it-smart-retries&quot;&gt;U02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/change-price&quot;&gt;F47&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment is not proof of attendance, useful service or accepted work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3424" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-06.5-06.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="06.5" target="06.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-07" name="07 Resolve exceptions and protect value">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;07 / Resolve exceptions and protect value&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Handle returns, refunds, disputes and fraud fairly while limiting avoidable loss.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns contested/reversed transactions and loss protection, including transaction-fraud decisions before payment. Failed payment execution is 05; failed delivery prevention is 06; future relationship retention is 09.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;7A. Return eligibility and diagnosis&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to understand what went wrong and resolve it consistently without punishing honest customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Return decision / refund liability / reverse movement&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-07.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="07.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.1.1 · Return requests arrive across channels with incomplete order details&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Create one case tied to the order, item, reason and policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original payment, refundable balance and reversal history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item identity, return policy, condition, reasons, pickup and inspection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join evidence to a return case and estimate the financial effect of valid resolutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate tickets; missing order IDs; return reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to first resolution; duplicate case rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent feedback / refund APIs / integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Refund/order context exists; unified return intake is mainly integrated.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 4/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 4/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data cannot inspect goods or determine every commercial entitlement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.1-07.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.1" target="07.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.1.2 · Staff apply the return policy differently to similar customers&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make eligibility and approved exceptions clear and traceable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original payment, refundable balance and reversal history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item identity, return policy, condition, reasons, pickup and inspection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join evidence to a return case and estimate the financial effect of valid resolutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Policy version; case attributes; exception approvals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Inconsistent decisions; escalations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent feedback / refund APIs / integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Guardrails help permitted actions; policy adjudication needs product context.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 3/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 3/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data cannot inspect goods or determine every commercial entitlement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.1-07.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.1" target="07.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.1.3 · Generic return reasons hide a recurring quality or sizing defect&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Capture useful structured reasons and review product-level patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original payment, refundable balance and reversal history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item identity, return policy, condition, reasons, pickup and inspection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join evidence to a return case and estimate the financial effect of valid resolutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Reason text; SKU/batch; photos; defect incidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat defects; preventable return rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Agent feedback / refund APIs / integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Feedback can reveal patterns; root-cause quality investigation remains partial.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 3/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 3/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data cannot inspect goods or determine every commercial entitlement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.1-07.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.1" target="07.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.1.4 · A return is approved but reverse pickup and inspection are delayed&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track each stage until the item is inspected and the case resolved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original payment, refundable balance and reversal history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item identity, return policy, condition, reasons, pickup and inspection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Join evidence to a return case and estimate the financial effect of valid resolutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Pickup; inbound scan; inspection; case age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Return turnaround; recoverable stock value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Agent feedback / refund APIs / integrations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Refund execution does not control reverse pickup or inspection.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 3/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 3/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payment data cannot inspect goods or determine every commercial entitlement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.1-07.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.1" target="07.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;7B. Exchange and fair alternatives&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to preserve a useful customer relationship when another solution fits their actual need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Exchange / store-credit liability / refund alternatives&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-07.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="07.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.2.1 · A customer requests a refund for a fixable variant mismatch&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Offer an available, relevant exchange while preserving valid refund choice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid/refunded amount, credit issued and redemption if supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer preference, suitable available stock, margin and incentive cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Offer a consented exchange or refund and show net value after obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Return reason; replacement stock; exchange acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Net value retained after exchange costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Wallet refunds / Engage / linked returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wallet/refund partnerships support alternatives; suitability still matters.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 4/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 4/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Store credit is a liability until resolved under the applicable accounting treatment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.2-07.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.2" target="07.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.2.2 · An exchange recommendation suggests an unavailable or unsuitable item&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Use current stock and stated customer needs for recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid/refunded amount, credit issued and redemption if supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer preference, suitable available stock, margin and incentive cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Offer a consented exchange or refund and show net value after obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory freshness; suitability attributes; repeat returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Successful exchanges; second-return rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Wallet refunds / Engage / linked returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;An alternative needs live inventory; universal matching is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 3/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 3/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Store credit is a liability until resolved under the applicable accounting treatment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.2-07.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.2" target="07.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.2.3 · Store credit looks like recovered revenue even when it remains unused&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track credit liability, redemption and actual incremental repurchase separately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid/refunded amount, credit issued and redemption if supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer preference, suitable available stock, margin and incentive cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Offer a consented exchange or refund and show net value after obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Credits issued/redeemed/expired; associated orders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Redeemed contribution; outstanding credit liability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Wallet refunds / Engage / linked returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Credit records help; profit and liability treatment need accounting.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 3/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 3/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Store credit is a liability until resolved under the applicable accounting treatment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.2-07.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.2" target="07.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.2.4 · Incentives to avoid refunds exceed the margin saved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare exchange/credit incentives with shipping, item and service costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Paid/refunded amount, credit issued and redemption if supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Customer preference, suitable available stock, margin and incentive cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Offer a consented exchange or refund and show net value after obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Incentive value; reverse logistics; retained margin.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Net retained contribution; customer satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Wallet refunds / Engage / linked returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Offer controls help; net-margin-aware optimization is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-d2c-brands-can-stop-losing-customers-at-the-refund-stage/&quot;&gt;R18&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Return Prime 2/5 — Thrive AI / returns&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Returns and exchange assistance to preserve suitable orders.&lt;br&gt;India / connected ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.returnprime.com/blog/introducing-thrive-ai-the-returns-revenue-engine-for-d2c-brands&quot;&gt;I06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Loop 2/5 — Returns / exchanges&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Return and exchange workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.loopreturns.com/launches/spring-2026/&quot;&gt;U12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Store credit is a liability until resolved under the applicable accounting treatment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.2-07.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.2" target="07.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;7C. Refund accuracy and communication&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to return the right amount once and give the customer a trustworthy status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Refund authorization / execution / status&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-07.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="07.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.3.1 · The refund amount is wrong after a partial return or bundled discount&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Calculate against the actual paid amount, item allocation and policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original transaction, refundable amount, refund ID, state and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item-level entitlement, discount allocation, support approvals and customer communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate an approved refund and communicate verified progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Original payment; discounts; returned items; previous refunds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Refund calculation errors; adjustment cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Refund APIs / dashboard / team controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial refund tools exist; bundle allocation needs order-level logic.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Refunds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Refund amount and state management linked to the original payment.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/refunds&quot;&gt;F11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Bank completion and the correct commercial amount are not fully controlled by the gateway.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.3-07.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.3" target="07.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.3.2 · Two staff members refund the same complaint&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Coordinate cases and check prior refund state before execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original transaction, refundable amount, refund ID, state and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item-level entitlement, discount allocation, support approvals and customer communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate an approved refund and communicate verified progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Refund IDs; case IDs; pending/processed amount.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate refunds; financial loss.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Refund APIs / dashboard / team controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Transaction limits help; safe concurrent approvals still need controls.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Refunds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Refund amount and state management linked to the original payment.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/refunds&quot;&gt;F11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Bank completion and the correct commercial amount are not fully controlled by the gateway.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="840" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.3-07.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.3" target="07.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.3.3 · The customer cannot see where a delayed refund is stuck&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide status, reference and appropriate escalation without inventing an arrival date.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original transaction, refundable amount, refund ID, state and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item-level entitlement, discount allocation, support approvals and customer communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate an approved refund and communicate verified progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Refund state; provider reference; elapsed time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Refund-related contacts; resolution time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Refund APIs / dashboard / team controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Status workflows directly help; bank delays remain possible.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Refunds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Refund amount and state management linked to the original payment.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/refunds&quot;&gt;F11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Bank completion and the correct commercial amount are not fully controlled by the gateway.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2497" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.3-07.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.3" target="07.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.3.4 · A refund approval waits because the merchant fears abuse&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Separate routine eligible refunds from cases needing evidence or approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Original transaction, refundable amount, refund ID, state and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Item-level entitlement, discount allocation, support approvals and customer communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Validate an approved refund and communicate verified progress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Policy eligibility; risk signals; approval queue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to refund; manual review yield.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Refund APIs / dashboard / team controls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Permissions help; fraud-versus-service judgment is not fully automated.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/refunds/&quot;&gt;F05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Refunds&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Refund amount and state management linked to the original payment.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/refunds&quot;&gt;F11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Retail POS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment, inventory and purchasing records.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/retail&quot;&gt;F13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/8258-create-purchase-orders-with-square-for-retail&quot;&gt;F18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Bank completion and the correct commercial amount are not fully controlled by the gateway.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3424" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.3-07.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.3" target="07.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;7D. Disputes and chargebacks&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to respond with accurate evidence before deadlines and learn why disputes happen.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute evidence / chargeback management&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-07.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="07.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.4.1 · A dispute deadline passes while evidence sits in several tools&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Gather order, payment, delivery and communication records into one case.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute reason, deadline, payment authentication and submitted evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery/usage proof, customer communications, policy acceptance and response cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble evidence, recommend contest or accept, and track repeated causes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Deadline; missing evidence; connector status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; On-time response; avoidable default losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Dispute workflows / Agent Studio&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specialist dispute preparation is described; evidence completeness remains conditional.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Smart Disputes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Dispute evidence and response automation.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management&quot;&gt;U04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Winning remains the issuer/network decision; strongest evidence is often external.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.4-07.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.4" target="07.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.4.2 · I spend more fighting a weak dispute than its recoverable value&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Assess eligibility, evidence quality, cost and win uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute reason, deadline, payment authentication and submitted evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery/usage proof, customer communications, policy acceptance and response cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble evidence, recommend contest or accept, and track repeated causes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute amount/reason; evidence; handling cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Net dispute recovery; time per case.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Dispute workflows / Agent Studio&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No complete expected-net-value decision engine was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Smart Disputes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Dispute evidence and response automation.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management&quot;&gt;U04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 1/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Winning remains the issuer/network decision; strongest evidence is often external.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.4-07.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.4" target="07.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.4.3 · A customer does not recognize the billing description&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make charge identity and purchase details easy to verify.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute reason, deadline, payment authentication and submitted evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery/usage proof, customer communications, policy acceptance and response cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble evidence, recommend contest or accept, and track repeated causes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Unrecognized-charge reasons; descriptor; receipts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Avoidable disputes; inquiry resolution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Dispute workflows / Agent Studio&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment and support context can help; descriptor configuration must be checked.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Smart Disputes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Dispute evidence and response automation.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management&quot;&gt;U04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 1/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Winning remains the issuer/network decision; strongest evidence is often external.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.4-07.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.4" target="07.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.4.4 · The same underlying issue keeps generating new chargebacks&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Link dispute reasons to product, fulfillment or billing defects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Dispute reason, deadline, payment authentication and submitted evidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery/usage proof, customer communications, policy acceptance and response cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble evidence, recommend contest or accept, and track repeated causes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Reason codes; cohorts; affected products; recurring failures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat dispute incidence; root-cause fixes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Dispute workflows / Agent Studio&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Case data exposes repetition; fixing underlying fulfillment needs other teams.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/how-to-use-razorpay-dashboard/&quot;&gt;F04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Smart Disputes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Dispute evidence and response automation.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management&quot;&gt;U04&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gorgias 2/5 — AI customer support&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Order-aware customer support and permitted actions.&lt;br&gt;Global / supported ecommerce · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gorgias.com/en-US/ai-agent-explained-497772&quot;&gt;U13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Winning remains the issuer/network decision; strongest evidence is often external.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.4-07.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.4" target="07.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;7E. Fraud, abuse and fair review&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to stop real losses while protecting legitimate sales and customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Transaction fraud / abuse / review&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-07.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="07.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.5.1 · Stolen credentials or automated attacks create risky payments&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Screen relevant risk signals and use proportionate verification.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment velocity, authentication, instrument/device risk and disputes in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Promotion histories, returns, account identity and manually reviewed outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Flag risk, apply bounded controls and measure false declines alongside losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Transaction patterns; device/risk signals; later confirmed fraud.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Fraud loss; legitimate acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Shield cross-border / exporter risk dashboard / COD risk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Shield and risk controls address specified flows; exporter scope is not universal domestic coverage.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/built-in-payment-gateway-fraud-detection-india/&quot;&gt;F43&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Radar&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payment-risk detection, review and configurable rules.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;U03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 3/5 — RiskShield&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment risk monitoring and configurable fraud controls.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/news-room/cashfree-payments-launches-riskshield-to-empower-merchants-curb-cyber-payment-frauds-in-real-time/&quot;&gt;F45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Scores are uncertain; permissions and sensitive attributes require careful handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.5-07.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.5" target="07.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.5.2 · Strict risk rules reject good customers and I cannot see the tradeoff&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Measure false positives and allow controlled review or alternate verification.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment velocity, authentication, instrument/device risk and disputes in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Promotion histories, returns, account identity and manually reviewed outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Flag risk, apply bounded controls and measure false declines alongside losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Declines; appeals; verified good outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Good sales lost; loss prevented.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Shield cross-border / exporter risk dashboard / COD risk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Controls exist; transparent lost-sales tradeoffs need outcome measurement.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/built-in-payment-gateway-fraud-detection-india/&quot;&gt;F43&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Radar&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment-risk detection, review and configurable rules.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;U03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 2/5 — RiskShield&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment risk monitoring and configurable fraud controls.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/news-room/cashfree-payments-launches-riskshield-to-empower-merchants-curb-cyber-payment-frauds-in-real-time/&quot;&gt;F45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Scores are uncertain; permissions and sensitive attributes require careful handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.5-07.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.5" target="07.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.5.3 · Repeated coupon or return abuse escapes separate systems&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Connect permitted account, order and return histories with human review.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment velocity, authentication, instrument/device risk and disputes in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Promotion histories, returns, account identity and manually reviewed outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Flag risk, apply bounded controls and measure false declines alongside losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Repeated incentives; return ratios; linked cases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Confirmed abuse loss; mistaken accusations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Shield cross-border / exporter risk dashboard / COD risk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Separated commerce systems limit cross-channel abuse detection.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/built-in-payment-gateway-fraud-detection-india/&quot;&gt;F43&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Radar&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment-risk detection, review and configurable rules.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;U03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 1/5 — RiskShield&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Payment risk monitoring and configurable fraud controls.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/news-room/cashfree-payments-launches-riskshield-to-empower-merchants-curb-cyber-payment-frauds-in-real-time/&quot;&gt;F45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Scores are uncertain; permissions and sensitive attributes require careful handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.5-07.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.5" target="07.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="07.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;07.5.4 · Fraud detection gives a score without an actionable explanation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Show the evidence, uncertainty and permitted decision choices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment velocity, authentication, instrument/device risk and disputes in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Promotion histories, returns, account identity and manually reviewed outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Flag risk, apply bounded controls and measure false declines alongside losses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Risk reasons; missing data; reviewer decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Review quality; time per decision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Shield cross-border / exporter risk dashboard / COD risk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Risk inputs help; explanations and appeal outcomes need checking.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/magic-checkout/&quot;&gt;R10&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agent-studio-principles-guardrails-and-merchant-control/&quot;&gt;R03&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/built-in-payment-gateway-fraud-detection-india/&quot;&gt;F43&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Radar&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payment-risk detection, review and configurable rules.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;U03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cashfree 2/5 — RiskShield&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payment risk monitoring and configurable fraud controls.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cashfree.com/news-room/cashfree-payments-launches-riskshield-to-empower-merchants-curb-cyber-payment-frauds-in-real-time/&quot;&gt;F45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Scores are uncertain; permissions and sensitive attributes require careful handling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-07.5-07.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="07.5" target="07.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-08" name="08 Receive, reconcile and account for money">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;08 / Receive, reconcile and account for money&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Know where collected money is, match it to business records and produce trustworthy accounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns settlement, remittance, matching, fee audit and financial/tax records. Unpaid customer obligations are 05; cash allocation and financing decisions are 10.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;8A. Settlement and remittance visibility&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know when collected money will become available and why something is delayed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Settlement / remittance / currency receipt&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-08.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="08.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.1.1 · Sales are successful but the money is not yet in my bank&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Distinguish authorized, captured, pending settlement and bank-received states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Captured amounts, settlement batches, payout state, deductions and FX in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank credits, marketplace/courier remittance, bank holidays and contracted terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace a collection to usable bank cash and isolate the blocking party.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Settlement schedule; capture date; bank credit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unexpected settlement delay; forecast accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Settlements / Smart Collect / international transfers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Settlement tracking directly addresses own-rail cash visibility.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 4/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A provider usually sees only its own settlement rail without additional connections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.1-08.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.1" target="08.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.1.2 · A payout is held or fails without a clear owner for resolution&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; See the actual status, requested evidence and next escalation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Captured amounts, settlement batches, payout state, deductions and FX in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank credits, marketplace/courier remittance, bank holidays and contracted terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace a collection to usable bank cash and isolate the blocking party.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Hold reason; bank details; settlement failure events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to release/resolve; unresolved balance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Settlements / Smart Collect / international transfers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Failure states help; bank/provider resolution may still require support.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 3/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A provider usually sees only its own settlement rail without additional connections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.1-08.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.1" target="08.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.1.3 · COD cash collected by the courier is not remitted as expected&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Match delivered COD orders with carrier collection and remittance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Captured amounts, settlement batches, payout state, deductions and FX in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank credits, marketplace/courier remittance, bank holidays and contracted terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace a collection to usable bank cash and isolate the blocking party.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery proof; COD ledger; remittance batches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Overdue COD receivable; missing cash.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Settlements / Smart Collect / international transfers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No complete native courier-COD remittance workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 1/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A provider usually sees only its own settlement rail without additional connections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.1-08.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.1" target="08.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.1.4 · International receipts arrive net of unfamiliar conversions and deductions&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track original currency, conversion, fees and net bank credit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Captured amounts, settlement batches, payout state, deductions and FX in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank credits, marketplace/courier remittance, bank holidays and contracted terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Trace a collection to usable bank cash and isolate the blocking party.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; FX rate; payment advice; bank statement; fee detail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unexplained FX/fee variance; remittance matching.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Settlements / Smart Collect / international transfers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;International collection disclosures help; currency and fee coverage varies.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 4/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A provider usually sees only its own settlement rail without additional connections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.1-08.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.1" target="08.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;8B. Transaction matching&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need one traceable chain from order to payment to settlement to bank.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Reconciliation / account references / accounting joins&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-08.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="08.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.2.1 · One bank deposit contains hundreds of sales and deductions&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Break settlement batches into their underlying transactions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment, refund, dispute, settlement IDs and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Invoices, bank statements, marketplace exports and accounting-period rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match known flows, explain residual differences and route exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Settlement IDs; transaction reports; bank credits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unmatched value; reconciliation time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Smart Collect / settlement reports / AP ERP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Own-rail settlement breakdowns support batch matching.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 4/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Automatic matching needs stable identifiers; ambiguous matches should remain reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.2-08.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.2" target="08.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.2.2 · A bank transfer arrives without an invoice reference&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Identify the payer and obligation without guessing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment, refund, dispute, settlement IDs and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Invoices, bank statements, marketplace exports and accounting-period rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match known flows, explain residual differences and route exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Customer identifiers; remittance advice; amount/date matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unallocated cash; incorrect allocations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — Smart Collect / settlement reports / AP ERP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Virtual collection identifiers support invoice-linked bank transfer receipt.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 4/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Automatic matching needs stable identifiers; ambiguous matches should remain reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.2-08.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.2" target="08.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.2.3 · Refunds and disputes appear in a later period than the sale&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Link reversals to originals while preserving accounting dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment, refund, dispute, settlement IDs and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Invoices, bank statements, marketplace exports and accounting-period rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match known flows, explain residual differences and route exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Original IDs; reversal dates; settlement adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unexplained period differences; adjustment accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Smart Collect / settlement reports / AP ERP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Event records help; cross-period accounting policy remains external.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 4/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 3/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Automatic matching needs stable identifiers; ambiguous matches should remain reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.2-08.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.2" target="08.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.2.4 · Marketplaces and gateways use incompatible formats and identifiers&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Normalize records and route ambiguous matches for review.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment, refund, dispute, settlement IDs and references.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Invoices, bank statements, marketplace exports and accounting-period rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Match known flows, explain residual differences and route exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Files/APIs; order references; duplicate/missing fields.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Auto-match quality; exception backlog.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Smart Collect / settlement reports / AP ERP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Multiple formats need a broader reconciliation layer than gateway reporting.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/smart-collect/&quot;&gt;R14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 2/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Automatic matching needs stable identifiers; ambiguous matches should remain reviewable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.2-08.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.2" target="08.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;8C. Fees, deductions and leakage&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know whether every deduction is expected and justified.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Fee audit / deductions / settlement financing&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-08.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="08.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.3.1 · Processing fees differ from my agreed commercial terms&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare actual charges with the applicable contract and payment mix.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Observed provider fees, settlement adjustments and offered access charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Commercial contracts, courier weights, marketplace terms and bank alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare realized deductions with agreed terms and queue material mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Fee schedules; invoices; transaction attributes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incorrect fees identified and recovered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Settlement reports / AP / instant settlement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fee visibility exists; automated contract-to-fee auditing is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A report is not an independent audit of whether charges were commercially correct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.3-08.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.3" target="08.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.3.2 · Shipping or marketplace deductions are silently accepted&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Audit billed charges against shipment/order records and allowed terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Observed provider fees, settlement adjustments and offered access charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Commercial contracts, courier weights, marketplace terms and bank alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare realized deductions with agreed terms and queue material mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Weight disputes; commissions; penalties; contract terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Disputed deductions; net value recovered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Settlement reports / AP / instant settlement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AP can record charges; logistics and marketplace contesting need evidence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A report is not an independent audit of whether charges were commercially correct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.3-08.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.3" target="08.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.3.3 · Small unmatched amounts are repeatedly written off&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Aggregate recurring exceptions and investigate systemic causes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Observed provider fees, settlement adjustments and offered access charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Commercial contracts, courier weights, marketplace terms and bank alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare realized deductions with agreed terms and queue material mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Exception frequency; amount patterns; write-off reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Preventable write-offs; unresolved aging.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Settlement reports / AP / instant settlement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Matching helps find residuals; policy determines investigation versus write-off.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A report is not an independent audit of whether charges were commercially correct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2519" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.3-08.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.3" target="08.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.3.4 · Instant access to funds is offered without a clear cost comparison&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare speed, fee and actual cash need before choosing settlement options.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Observed provider fees, settlement adjustments and offered access charges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Commercial contracts, courier weights, marketplace terms and bank alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare realized deductions with agreed terms and queue material mismatches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Available balance; timing; fees; upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Avoidable financing/settlement cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Settlement reports / AP / instant settlement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Access options exist; independent all-in financing comparison is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A report is not an independent audit of whether charges were commercially correct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3468" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.3-08.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.3" target="08.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;8D. Bookkeeping, tax and evidence&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need accurate records that my accountant can close without repeatedly asking me to reconstruct events.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Bookkeeping / tax evidence / revenue recognition&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-08.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="08.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.4.1 · Sales invoices, purchase records and tax data contain mismatches&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile documents and resolve missing or inconsistent entries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, payouts, invoices, reimbursements and settlement reports in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Ledger categories, tax registrations, obligations, delivered service and personal spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare reconciled evidence and explain cash versus earned revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice IDs; tax records; purchase/sales registers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unresolved mismatches; close rework.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Reports / AP integration / Payroll compliance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Connected records help; complete GST/bookkeeping is not a gateway feature.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 4/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 2/5 — Revenue Recognition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Revenue-recognition workflow from connected billing and transaction records.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/revenue-recognition&quot;&gt;U05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Tax/accounting decisions require the applicable rules and a complete ledger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.4-08.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.4" target="08.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.4.2 · Business and personal transactions are mixed together&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Classify transactions and retain supporting evidence consistently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, payouts, invoices, reimbursements and settlement reports in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Ledger categories, tax registrations, obligations, delivered service and personal spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare reconciled evidence and explain cash versus earned revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Accounts; receipts; owner transfers; categories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unclassified items; accountant rework.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Reports / AP integration / Payroll compliance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Business accounts assist separation; classification still needs user context.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 1/5 — Revenue Recognition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Revenue-recognition workflow from connected billing and transaction records.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/revenue-recognition&quot;&gt;U05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Tax/accounting decisions require the applicable rules and a complete ledger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.4-08.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.4" target="08.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.4.3 · Cash receipts are mistaken for earned revenue or profit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Separate collections, liabilities, earned revenue and costs appropriately.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, payouts, invoices, reimbursements and settlement reports in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Ledger categories, tax registrations, obligations, delivered service and personal spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare reconciled evidence and explain cash versus earned revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Subscription periods; advances; credit balances; ledger rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Revenue accuracy; unexplained balance changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Reports / AP integration / Payroll compliance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sales summaries do not establish an accrual-revenue system.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 4/5 — Revenue Recognition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Revenue-recognition workflow from connected billing and transaction records.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/revenue-recognition&quot;&gt;U05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Tax/accounting decisions require the applicable rules and a complete ledger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.4-08.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.4" target="08.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.4.4 · Month-end work depends on missing receipts and manual exports&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Collect evidence continuously and preserve audit-ready links.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts, payouts, invoices, reimbursements and settlement reports in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Ledger categories, tax registrations, obligations, delivered service and personal spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare reconciled evidence and explain cash versus earned revenue.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Missing documents; export tasks; exception age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Days to close; manual close hours.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Reports / AP integration / Payroll compliance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;ERP and AP integrations reduce manual work; full close remains broader.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/settlements/&quot;&gt;R13&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 4/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stripe 3/5 — Revenue Recognition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Revenue-recognition workflow from connected billing and transaction records.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/revenue-recognition&quot;&gt;U05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Tax/accounting decisions require the applicable rules and a complete ledger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.4-08.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.4" target="08.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;8E. Decision-ready financial understanding&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need consistent numbers and explanations that help me decide what to do next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Financial intelligence / revenue diagnosis&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-08.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="08.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.5.1 · Two dashboards report different revenue for the same period&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Expose definitions, time zones, taxes, refunds and recognition basis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions, settlement timing, fees and bank records if connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory, channel demand, order delivery, cost ledger and reporting definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile definitions and explain changes with evidence and uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Metric definitions; date ranges; included statuses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Reporting variance; reconciliation effort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RAY / RazorpayX cashflow / BillMe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Conversational access helps; cross-system revenue definitions need alignment.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; An AI narrative cannot recover missing data or prove causation from correlations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.5-08.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.5" target="08.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.5.2 · Revenue falls but I cannot separate demand loss from payment or delivery failure&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Break changes into observable stages and avoid unsupported causal claims.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions, settlement timing, fees and bank records if connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory, channel demand, order delivery, cost ledger and reporting definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile definitions and explain changes with evidence and uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Funnel counts; success rates; stockouts; delivery outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to diagnose; confirmed causes addressed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — RAY / RazorpayX cashflow / BillMe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment root-cause analysis is described; delivery and demand require extra data.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; An AI narrative cannot recover missing data or prove causation from correlations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1592" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.5-08.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.5" target="08.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.5.3 · I see total sales but not net contribution by product or channel&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Connect costs and reversals to sales with stated allocation assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions, settlement timing, fees and bank records if connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory, channel demand, order delivery, cost ledger and reporting definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile definitions and explain changes with evidence and uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Net sales; product/fulfillment/channel costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Contribution visibility; loss-making segments found.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RAY / RazorpayX cashflow / BillMe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sales segmentation is useful; full net contribution needs product/channel costs.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; An AI narrative cannot recover missing data or prove causation from correlations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.5-08.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.5" target="08.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="08.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;08.5.4 · An AI summary gives an answer without showing the calculation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide underlying records, definitions and a reproducible calculation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Transactions, settlement timing, fees and bank records if connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Inventory, channel demand, order delivery, cost ledger and reporting definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile definitions and explain changes with evidence and uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Query lineage; inputs; excluded records; formula.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Answer verification; numerical error rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RAY / RazorpayX cashflow / BillMe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No universal evidence-linked calculation trail was verified for every AI answer.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/meet-ray-your-always-on-ai-account-manager-now-live-on-whatsapp/&quot;&gt;R04&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Square AI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Business questions and content assistance based on connected Square data.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/ai&quot;&gt;F17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; An AI narrative cannot recover missing data or prove causation from correlations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3468" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-08.5-08.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="08.5" target="08.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-09" name="09 Retain and grow existing relationships">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;09 / Retain and grow existing relationships&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Earn another useful, profitable purchase and keep customers who still value the offer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns post-purchase relationship, voluntary churn, loyalty, replenishment and expansion. Failed debits are 05; a live refund/dispute is 07; acquisition of genuinely new buyers is 03.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="4320" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;9A. Identity and relationship context&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to recognize the same customer and understand their actual experience before contacting them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Payment-linked identity / customer history&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-09.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="09.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.1.1 · The same customer appears as several people across store and website&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Resolve identity carefully and retain uncertainty where matching is weak.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Customer identifiers, order/receipt history and payment-linked profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store/website identities, complaints, consent and staff-owned notes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Build a permissioned relationship view and suppress inappropriate outreach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Contact IDs; purchase history; match confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate profiles; wrong-person personalization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — BillMe / Engage customer data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Unified customer records help; disconnected identifiers still need resolution.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 3/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Matching is imperfect; identity across merchants is not automatically permitted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.1-09.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.1" target="09.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.1.2 · I market to a customer without noticing an unresolved complaint&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Use current service context to pause or adapt relationship outreach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Customer identifiers, order/receipt history and payment-linked profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store/website identities, complaints, consent and staff-owned notes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Build a permissioned relationship view and suppress inappropriate outreach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Open support cases; refund status; recent feedback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Insensitive outreach; complaint escalation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe / Engage customer data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Campaign context exists; complaint joins and suppression need verification.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Matching is imperfect; identity across merchants is not automatically permitted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.1-09.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.1" target="09.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.1.3 · I cannot distinguish a regular buyer from a one-time gift purchaser&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand purchase purpose and repeat patterns without inventing intent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Customer identifiers, order/receipt history and payment-linked profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store/website identities, complaints, consent and staff-owned notes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Build a permissioned relationship view and suppress inappropriate outreach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Product mix; timing; gift indicators; customer responses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Segment usefulness; irrelevant messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe / Engage customer data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Purchase segmentation helps; motive requires more than receipt frequency.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 2/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Matching is imperfect; identity across merchants is not automatically permitted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.1-09.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.1" target="09.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.1.4 · Customer history disappears when a staff member leaves&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Keep shared relationship notes with appropriate access and consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Customer identifiers, order/receipt history and payment-linked profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Store/website identities, complaints, consent and staff-owned notes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Build a permissioned relationship view and suppress inappropriate outreach.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Unlogged conversations; account ownership; missing context.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat explanations; handover time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — BillMe / Engage customer data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A shared platform preserves recorded history, not unrecorded staff knowledge.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 2/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Matching is imperfect; identity across merchants is not automatically permitted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.1-09.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.1" target="09.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;9B. Replenishment and repeat timing&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to be helpful at the right moment without discounting customers who would return anyway.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat purchase / replenishment timing&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-09.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="09.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.2.1 · I do not know when a customer is likely to need the product again&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate a reorder window using sufficient relevant history and uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase intervals, spend, category and customer ID in the merchant footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU consumption, gifts, off-platform purchases, stock and consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate a repeat window and test whether a reminder adds useful purchases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order intervals; product/quantity; seasonality.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental repeat contribution; timing accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe Auto Engagement / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Automated journeys exist; individual next-order prediction is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 4/5 — Predictive analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Predictive customer timing and value from connected commerce data.&lt;br&gt;Global / data-eligible merchants · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A prediction is not certainty; non-purchase outside the footprint is unobserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.2-09.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.2" target="09.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.2.2 · Everyone receives the same reminder despite different buying patterns&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Adapt timing to customer and product context when data supports it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase intervals, spend, category and customer ID in the merchant footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU consumption, gifts, off-platform purchases, stock and consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate a repeat window and test whether a reminder adds useful purchases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Customer cadence; prior response; message history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Repeat conversion versus baseline; opt-outs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — BillMe Auto Engagement / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Segmentation/journeys are supported; advanced timing precision needs evidence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 4/5 — Predictive analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Predictive customer timing and value from connected commerce data.&lt;br&gt;Global / data-eligible merchants · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A prediction is not certainty; non-purchase outside the footprint is unobserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.2-09.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.2" target="09.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.2.3 · Customers have not returned but I do not know why&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Ask or infer cautiously among timing, product fit, price and service issues.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase intervals, spend, category and customer ID in the merchant footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU consumption, gifts, off-platform purchases, stock and consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate a repeat window and test whether a reminder adds useful purchases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Feedback; return reasons; purchase gap; support history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Explained lapse reasons; useful follow-up rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe Auto Engagement / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Dormancy signals help; why a customer left remains uncertain.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 3/5 — Predictive analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Predictive customer timing and value from connected commerce data.&lt;br&gt;Global / data-eligible merchants · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A prediction is not certainty; non-purchase outside the footprint is unobserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.2-09.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.2" target="09.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.2.4 · A campaign promotes a refill the customer already bought elsewhere in my business&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Check recent purchases across connected channels before sending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase intervals, spend, category and customer ID in the merchant footprint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; SKU consumption, gifts, off-platform purchases, stock and consent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate a repeat window and test whether a reminder adds useful purchases.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Latest order; channel sync; queued messages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Redundant prompts; wasted incentives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — BillMe Auto Engagement / Engage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Linked histories help suppress duplicates; unconnected channels remain blind spots.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 3/5 — Predictive analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Predictive customer timing and value from connected commerce data.&lt;br&gt;Global / data-eligible merchants · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 3/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A prediction is not certainty; non-purchase outside the footprint is unobserved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.2-09.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.2" target="09.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;9C. Loyalty and incentives&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need loyalty spending to build durable relationships and remain understandable to customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Loyalty / incentives / reward liabilities&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-09.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="09.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.3.1 · Rewards are confusing, unavailable or difficult to redeem&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Make balance, eligibility, expiry and redemption clear.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Earned points, redemptions, payment history and campaign outcomes where integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Offer costs, margins, true customer responsiveness and control groups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Simplify rewards and test smaller incentives against a no-incentive baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Redemption errors; unused balance; support contacts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Successful redemption; loyalty complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — Engage / BillMe loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Loyalty tooling directly helps enrollment and redemption.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 4/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 2/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Redemption or repeat-purchase correlation does not prove the reward caused it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.3-09.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.3" target="09.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.3.2 · I give the largest discount to customers who need no incentive&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Test no-offer and lower-cost actions before assuming discount necessity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Earned points, redemptions, payment history and campaign outcomes where integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Offer costs, margins, true customer responsiveness and control groups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Simplify rewards and test smaller incentives against a no-incentive baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Purchase propensity; experiment outcomes; offer cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental contribution; discount avoided.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / BillMe loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Segmentation helps targeting; incremental incentive need is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Redemption or repeat-purchase correlation does not prove the reward caused it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.3-09.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.3" target="09.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.3.3 · Frequent promotions train customers to wait for the next sale&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Track dependence on discounts and test other sources of value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Earned points, redemptions, payment history and campaign outcomes where integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Offer costs, margins, true customer responsiveness and control groups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Simplify rewards and test smaller incentives against a no-incentive baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Full-price share; interpurchase gaps; promo history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Full-price contribution; long-run repeat rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Promotion tools do not by themselves prevent discount dependence.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Redemption or repeat-purchase correlation does not prove the reward caused it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2541" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.3-09.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.3" target="09.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.3.4 · My loyalty program earns points but does not change behavior&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Evaluate incremental visits and profit, accounting for reward obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Earned points, redemptions, payment history and campaign outcomes where integrated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Offer costs, margins, true customer responsiveness and control groups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Simplify rewards and test smaller incentives against a no-incentive baseline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Rewards issued/redeemed; control outcomes; contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental loyalty contribution; reward liability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Engage / BillMe loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Program metrics help; randomized behavioral impact needs a design.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/everything-you-need-to-know-about-razorpaybillme/&quot;&gt;R08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adyen 1/5 — Unified commerce insights / loyalty inputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects payment-derived shopper insights and loyalty identification.&lt;br&gt;Global supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.adyen.com/knowledge/unified-commerce/insights/how-can-i-view-my-shopper-insights&quot;&gt;F38&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.adyen.com/unified-commerce/loyalty-program/payment-linked-loyalty/&quot;&gt;F39&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Redemption or repeat-purchase correlation does not prove the reward caused it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3490" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.3-09.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.3" target="09.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;9D. Voluntary churn and expansion&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to understand why a customer wants to leave and offer a suitable choice without trapping them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Voluntary retention / subscription change / account expansion&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-09.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="09.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.4.1 · A subscriber cancels because they need a pause, not a permanent exit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Offer an appropriate approved pause or plan option with a clear cancel route.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Renewal, plan, invoice and payment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Usage, satisfaction, cancellation reasons, account health and customer preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Present a suitable pause/change or account-review action under merchant policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cancellation reason; usage; billing cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Retained value after costs; later satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Subscriptions / Engage / feedback agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Billing state can change; personalized cancellation-save orchestration is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A saved subscription without customer value can create complaints rather than growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="906" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.4-09.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.4" target="09.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.4.2 · An unused plan keeps renewing until the customer becomes angry&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Recognize low engagement and help customers understand or change their plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Renewal, plan, invoice and payment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Usage, satisfaction, cancellation reasons, account health and customer preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Present a suitable pause/change or account-review action under merchant policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Product usage; support requests; renewal dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Active use; avoidable complaints and refunds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Subscriptions / Engage / feedback agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Renewal execution is covered; proactive unused-plan care needs usage data.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 1/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A saved subscription without customer value can create complaints rather than growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1636" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.4-09.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.4" target="09.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.4.3 · A satisfied customer could use another service but receives random upsells&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Recommend an expansion that fits observed needs and availability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Renewal, plan, invoice and payment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Usage, satisfaction, cancellation reasons, account health and customer preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Present a suitable pause/change or account-review action under merchant policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Current products; usage; explicit interest; eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental expansion contribution; acceptance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Subscriptions / Engage / feedback agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Targeted offers exist; suitability-aware expansion needs more context.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A saved subscription without customer value can create complaints rather than growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2585" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.4-09.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.4" target="09.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.4.4 · A key business customer quietly reduces orders before leaving&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Notice changes and equip the relationship owner with context.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Renewal, plan, invoice and payment history.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Usage, satisfaction, cancellation reasons, account health and customer preferences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Present a suitable pause/change or account-review action under merchant policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order cadence; volume; complaints; contract dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Account retention; preventable contraction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Subscriptions / Engage / feedback agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Purchase trends help; B2B account-health intervention is not fully verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/docs/payments/subscriptions/&quot;&gt;F06&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agent-studio/&quot;&gt;R02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Square 2/5 — Customer Directory / Marketing / Loyalty&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects customer purchase history, audience groups and loyalty workflows.&lt;br&gt;US edition · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/customer-directory&quot;&gt;F14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/marketing&quot;&gt;F15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://squareup.com/us/en/software/loyalty&quot;&gt;F16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A saved subscription without customer value can create complaints rather than growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3534" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.4-09.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.4" target="09.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;9E. Incrementality and learning&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need evidence that contacting customers changed the outcome, not just that a sale happened afterward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental value / experimental learning&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-09.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="09.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.5.1 · A campaign claims every later purchase as recovered revenue&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare with a credible untreated baseline and avoid duplicate attribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique purchases, refunds, campaign actions and collected amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Random assignment, untreated baseline, product costs, opt-outs and long-term outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare no action, reminder and offer on net incremental contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Randomized holdout where feasible; order linkage; time window.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental orders and contribution with uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe campaign measurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Campaign sales metrics exist; causal recovery accounting is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 1/5 — Predictive customer analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Customer-level prediction can inform treatment selection.&lt;br&gt;Global / eligible data · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Do not confuse attribution with causality; small samples may be inconclusive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.5-09.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.5" target="09.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.5.2 · The best message by clicks is not the best by profit&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Evaluate final orders, refunds, incentives and communication costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique purchases, refunds, campaign actions and collected amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Random assignment, untreated baseline, product costs, opt-outs and long-term outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare no action, reminder and offer on net incremental contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Delivery/click/order events; costs; delayed returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Incremental net contribution per eligible customer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe campaign measurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Engagement and sales reporting do not fully optimize net contribution.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 3/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 1/5 — Predictive customer analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Customer-level prediction can inform treatment selection.&lt;br&gt;Global / eligible data · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Do not confuse attribution with causality; small samples may be inconclusive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.5-09.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.5" target="09.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.5.3 · I cannot compare doing nothing, reminding and offering a discount&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Test permitted actions on comparable customers at sufficient sample size.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique purchases, refunds, campaign actions and collected amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Random assignment, untreated baseline, product costs, opt-outs and long-term outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare no action, reminder and offer on net incremental contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Assigned action; eligibility; outcomes; confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Action-specific uplift; decision uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe campaign measurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No complete documented randomized three-way profit test was found.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 4/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 1/5 — Predictive customer analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Customer-level prediction can inform treatment selection.&lt;br&gt;Global / eligible data · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Do not confuse attribution with causality; small samples may be inconclusive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.5-09.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.5" target="09.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;09.5.4 · An apparent short-term win causes later opt-outs or discount dependence&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Observe longer-term effects before scaling the action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Unique purchases, refunds, campaign actions and collected amounts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Random assignment, untreated baseline, product costs, opt-outs and long-term outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Compare no action, reminder and offer on net incremental contribution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Opt-outs; repeat rate; full-price share; complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Long-term contribution; customer harm signals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Engage / BillMe campaign measurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Long-run opt-outs and discount effects are not established as a closed loop.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/engage/&quot;&gt;R07&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/personalized-marketing-journeys/&quot;&gt;R09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chargebee 2/5 — Billing / Growth / Retention&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Subscription retention and measurement, including configured control groups.&lt;br&gt;Global / subscription businesses · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/growth/retention/&quot;&gt;F32&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/reporting/dashboards-trends&quot;&gt;F33&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/docs/growth/plays/plays-overview&quot;&gt;U11&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/billing/&quot;&gt;F46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Klaviyo 1/5 — Predictive customer analytics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Customer-level prediction can inform treatment selection.&lt;br&gt;Global / eligible data · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/ai/predictive-analytics-for-ecommerce&quot;&gt;U10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Do not confuse attribution with causality; small samples may be inconclusive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-09.5-09.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="09.5" target="09.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="bucket-10" name="10 Fund and sustain business operations">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="root" value="&lt;h1&gt;10 / Fund and sustain business operations&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Have enough affordable cash, people and operating discipline to keep promises and grow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Owns liquidity planning, financing, supplier/staff payments, recurring spend and business resource allocation. Supply selection is 02; customer collections 05; accounting facts 08; permissions and continuity controls 01. Insurance risk transfer and treasury policy also live here; transaction disputes remain in 07.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read scores:&lt;/b&gt; 0 no direct support identified; 1 enabling; 2 partial; 3 substantial; 4 strong; 5 mostly addressed with outcome evidence. No 5 assigned. All scores are analyst estimates, not percentages solved. Original 200 hypotheses plus 8 insurance/treasury additions; 95 public sources, reviewed 13 October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data:&lt;/b&gt; Native visibility depends on using the relevant financial product. External records need permitted access. Outcomes and availability are unverified for any particular merchant.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f1e8;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="0" width="6060" height="310" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10A. Cash visibility and planning&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know whether I can meet my next obligations without confusing sales, profit and usable cash.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Connected banking / cash forecasting&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.1.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.1.1 · I have money across accounts but no reliable available-cash view&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Combine usable balances and identify restricted or already-committed funds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Cleared and available balances, transactions and scheduled payouts where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Open receivables, payroll, purchase commitments, returns and financing repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a cash runway view and stress-test upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Bank balances; pending payments; reserves; scheduled payouts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Available-cash accuracy; unexpected shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — RazorpayX connected banking / cashflow agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Connected banking addresses the view; supported accounts and beta access vary.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 2/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 3/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Pending receipts are not spendable cash; forecasts require reconciled assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.1-10.1.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.1" target="10.1.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.1.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.1.2 · Payroll and supplier bills fall due before customer cash arrives&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Forecast inflows/outflows with timing uncertainty and actionable scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Cleared and available balances, transactions and scheduled payouts where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Open receivables, payroll, purchase commitments, returns and financing repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a cash runway view and stress-test upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Receivables; settlements; COD; payroll; bill dates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Cash shortfall days; forecast error.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — RazorpayX connected banking / cashflow agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cashflow insights help planning; full obligation coverage needs integrations.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 2/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 3/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Pending receipts are not spendable cash; forecasts require reconciled assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.1-10.1.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.1" target="10.1.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.1.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.1.3 · A large order looks like growth but requires cash before collection&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Model inventory, delivery and credit terms before committing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Cleared and available balances, transactions and scheduled payouts where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Open receivables, payroll, purchase commitments, returns and financing repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a cash runway view and stress-test upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Order margin; upfront costs; payment schedule.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Peak funding gap; cash-adjusted order viability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RazorpayX connected banking / cashflow agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Forecasting can expose a gap; purchase-order financing is a separate capability.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 1/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 3/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Pending receipts are not spendable cash; forecasts require reconciled assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.1-10.1.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.1" target="10.1.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.1.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.1.4 · Forecasts ignore returns, delayed invoices or a weaker sales week&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Stress-test realistic downside cases and show assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Cleared and available balances, transactions and scheduled payouts where connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Open receivables, payroll, purchase commitments, returns and financing repayments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a cash runway view and stress-test upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Delay distributions; refund patterns; demand scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Forecast resilience; avoided emergency borrowing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RazorpayX connected banking / cashflow agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI forecasts still need explicit downside scenarios and complete liabilities.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/newsroom/for-the-first-time-in-india-businesses-on-razorpayx-can-now-bank-with-ai-agents-that-work-while-they-sleep/&quot;&gt;R06&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plaid 1/5 — Financial data APIs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Supplies authorized bank balances, transactions and verification inputs.&lt;br&gt;US / supported markets · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://plaid.com/products/&quot;&gt;F20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 2/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Pending receipts are not spendable cash; forecasts require reconciled assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="0" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.1-10.1.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.1" target="10.1.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10B. Access to suitable finance&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need enough funding at terms I understand and can repay under realistic sales conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Credit access / underwriting / finance comparison&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.2.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.2.1 · I cannot buy stock because sales cash is locked in receivables&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare suitable invoice, order or working-capital options where eligible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment history, settlement cashflow and existing repayments in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank/GST records, receivables quality, purpose, credit offers and existing debt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble an application, compare repayment scenarios and flag cash shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Receivable quality; purchase orders; funding gap.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Orders funded; total financing cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards; historical Capital lending evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Credit product presence helps; current broad working-capital availability is uncertain.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 4/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 4/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only an authorized lender approves credit; funding is not proof a plan is viable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.2-10.2.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.2" target="10.2.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.2.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.2.2 · Loan applications require records scattered across tools&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare consistent financial evidence without repeated manual reconstruction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment history, settlement cashflow and existing repayments in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank/GST records, receivables quality, purpose, credit offers and existing debt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble an application, compare repayment scenarios and flag cash shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Bank/payment history; accounts; required documents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Application effort; time to decision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards; historical Capital lending evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Historical transaction-based prefill exists; current eligibility needs confirmation.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 3/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 3/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only an authorized lender approves credit; funding is not proof a plan is viable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.2-10.2.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.2" target="10.2.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.2.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.2.3 · An advertised rate hides the true effect on my cashflow&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand total repayment, fees, timing and adverse sales scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment history, settlement cashflow and existing repayments in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank/GST records, receivables quality, purpose, credit offers and existing debt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble an application, compare repayment scenarios and flag cash shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Repayment schedule; fees; revenue-linked deductions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Affordable debt service; effective total cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards; historical Capital lending evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Published product terms help; a neutral all-in comparison is not verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 2/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 2/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only an authorized lender approves credit; funding is not proof a plan is viable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.2-10.2.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.2" target="10.2.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.2.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.2.4 · I borrow for growth that never earns enough to repay the cost&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Test demand and contribution assumptions before taking on funding.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Payment history, settlement cashflow and existing repayments in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Bank/GST records, receivables quality, purpose, credit offers and existing debt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble an application, compare repayment scenarios and flag cash shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Growth scenario; unit economics; cash sensitivity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Return on funded activity; repayment stress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Corporate cards; historical Capital lending evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Credit access does not validate incremental operating returns.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low–medium: rollout or access needs validation&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://d6xcmfyh68wv8.cloudfront.net/docs/x/capital/working-capital-loans/&quot;&gt;F03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;CredAble 2/5 — Working-capital programs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Finances eligible payables, receivables and purchase-order needs.&lt;br&gt;India / partner programs · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/&quot;&gt;F41&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://credable.in/pre-shipment-financing-platform-for-banks/&quot;&gt;I09&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;KredX 2/5 — Supply-chain finance / cash management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Factoring, trade finance and cash-management workflows.&lt;br&gt;India / program eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kredx.com/&quot;&gt;F29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Only an authorized lender approves credit; funding is not proof a plan is viable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="870" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.2-10.2.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.2" target="10.2.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10C. Supplier and operating payments&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to pay the right counterparty the right amount at the right time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Accounts payable / supplier payment / discounting&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.3.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.3.1 · Supplier invoices arrive in email and chat and are missed&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Capture obligations centrally and assign approval owners.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice intake, verified payee, approval state, payment status and PO matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier contracts, cash forecasts, dispute status and early-payment offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare approved payments, flag duplicates and compare timing economics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoices; due dates; missing approvals; reminders.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Late fees; overdue payables; handling time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — AP Automation / payouts / vendor verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Invoice intake centralizes the workflow; adoption still matters.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 4/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A valid invoice does not authorize automatic payment outside merchant limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.3-10.3.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.3" target="10.3.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.3.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.3.2 · The same supplier bill is paid twice or against wrong bank details&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Check duplicates and verify changes before disbursement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice intake, verified payee, approval state, payment status and PO matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier contracts, cash forecasts, dispute status and early-payment offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare approved payments, flag duplicates and compare timing economics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice identifiers; beneficiary changes; prior payments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Duplicate/wrong payments; prevented loss.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — AP Automation / payouts / vendor verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Matching and verification address duplicates and payee errors.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 4/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A valid invoice does not authorize automatic payment outside merchant limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="1592" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.3-10.3.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.3" target="10.3.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.3.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.3.3 · Approval delays damage supplier relationships or stop supply&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Route approvals based on policy and expose urgent blocked bills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice intake, verified payee, approval state, payment status and PO matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier contracts, cash forecasts, dispute status and early-payment offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare approved payments, flag duplicates and compare timing economics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Approval age; due dates; supplier holds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; On-time payments; supply interruptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — AP Automation / payouts / vendor verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Configurable approval workflows directly support routing and control.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 4/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A valid invoice does not authorize automatic payment outside merchant limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.3-10.3.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.3" target="10.3.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.3.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.3.4 · I pay early without knowing whether preserving cash is more valuable&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare approved discounts, due dates and cash needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice intake, verified payee, approval state, payment status and PO matches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Supplier contracts, cash forecasts, dispute status and early-payment offers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare approved payments, flag duplicates and compare timing economics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Early-payment terms; cash forecast; financing costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Net benefit from payment timing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — AP Automation / payouts / vendor verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment automation exists; cash-versus-discount optimization is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;BILL 2/5 — Accounts receivable / payable&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Invoice tracking, collection follow-up, approval and payment workflows.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-receivable/&quot;&gt;U14&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bill.com/product/accounts-payable&quot;&gt;F25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; A valid invoice does not authorize automatic payment outside merchant limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="1740" y="3468" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.3-10.3.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.3" target="10.3.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10D. People, payroll and everyday execution&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need a team I can schedule and pay accurately without spending every week fixing administration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll / reimbursement / employee financial benefits&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.4.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.4.1 · I cannot find or retain staff with the skills the business needs&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Understand role requirements, workload and avoidable sources of turnover.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Salary components, reimbursements and payroll payment status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, leave, commissions, benefit eligibility and employment changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile payable amounts, speed approved reimbursement and expose recurring admin work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Vacancies; turnover; overtime; employee feedback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unfilled role days; turnover cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — RazorpayX Payroll / corporate cards&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payroll supports the employment relationship; staffing quality is not solved.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gusto 2/5 — Payroll / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Payroll connected with time and employee administration.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/product/payroll/hourly&quot;&gt;F34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 2/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll software cannot guarantee recruitment, skill availability or staff retention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="665" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.4-10.4.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.4" target="10.4.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.4.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.4.2 · Attendance, leave and commissions produce payroll mistakes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile approved inputs before salary calculation and payment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Salary components, reimbursements and payroll payment status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, leave, commissions, benefit eligibility and employment changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile payable amounts, speed approved reimbursement and expose recurring admin work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance; leave; commission rules; payroll exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll corrections; on-time salary payment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 4/5 — RazorpayX Payroll / corporate cards&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payroll addresses salary computation from correct attendance inputs.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gusto 4/5 — Payroll / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Payroll connected with time and employee administration.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/product/payroll/hourly&quot;&gt;F34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 1/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll software cannot guarantee recruitment, skill availability or staff retention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcefdc;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="1592" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.4-10.4.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.4" target="10.4.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.4.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.4.3 · Employees pay business expenses and wait too long for reimbursement&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Provide a clear submission, evidence, approval and payment path.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Salary components, reimbursements and payroll payment status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, leave, commissions, benefit eligibility and employment changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile payable amounts, speed approved reimbursement and expose recurring admin work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Receipts; claims; approval/payment age.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Reimbursement turnaround; employee follow-ups.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — RazorpayX Payroll / corporate cards&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reimbursement and cards reduce delays; approval processes still matter.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gusto 3/5 — Payroll / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payroll connected with time and employee administration.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/product/payroll/hourly&quot;&gt;F34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 1/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll software cannot guarantee recruitment, skill availability or staff retention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="2519" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.4-10.4.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.4" target="10.4.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.4.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.4.4 · Routine administration leaves the owner no time to improve the business&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Identify repetitive tasks, assign ownership and automate only suitable work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Salary components, reimbursements and payroll payment status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Attendance, leave, commissions, benefit eligibility and employment changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Reconcile payable amounts, speed approved reimbursement and expose recurring admin work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Time diary; repeated tasks; backlog; exception rate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Owner hours reclaimed; essential tasks missed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 3/5 — RazorpayX Payroll / corporate cards&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Finance administration is automated in parts, not all owner responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/payroll/founder/&quot;&gt;R16&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gusto 3/5 — Payroll / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Payroll connected with time and employee administration.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gusto.com/product/payroll/hourly&quot;&gt;F34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 2/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Payroll software cannot guarantee recruitment, skill availability or staff retention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Integration / execution gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dcecf3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2610" y="3446" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.4-10.4.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.4" target="10.4.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.5" value="&lt;h2&gt;10E. Sustainable growth and resource allocation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to choose which opportunities deserve scarce cash and attention, including when to stop.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data-enabled:&lt;/b&gt; Spend governance / resource allocation / financial exit&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.5">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.5.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.5.1 · Unused software, recurring fees and overlapping services accumulate&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Review utilization, renewals and cancellation consequences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Recurring charges, supplier commitments, debt and payment obligations in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Software usage, operating plans, lease/staff liabilities and closure obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize material cash leaks and compare scenarios before committing resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Vendor spend; usage; renewal dates; contract terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Avoidable recurring spend removed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards / AP / RAY / cashflow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spend reports and savings concierge help; usage-based SaaS cleanup is partial.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 4/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial optimization cannot decide the business strategy or discharge legal duties alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.5-10.5.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.5" target="10.5.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.5.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.5.2 · Many problems compete for attention and every dashboard says urgent&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize by business impact, controllability, effort and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Recurring charges, supplier commitments, debt and payment obligations in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Software usage, operating plans, lease/staff liabilities and closure obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize material cash leaks and compare scenarios before committing resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Backlogs; opportunity estimates; costs; dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Realized benefit per unit of effort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards / AP / RAY / cashflow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Insights help triage; a unified business priority optimizer is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 3/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 2/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial optimization cannot decide the business strategy or discharge legal duties alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.5-10.5.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.5" target="10.5.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.5.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.5.3 · Expansion to a second store or channel hides new fixed costs&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Model staffing, stock, rent, systems and demand before committing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Recurring charges, supplier commitments, debt and payment obligations in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Software usage, operating plans, lease/staff liabilities and closure obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize material cash leaks and compare scenarios before committing resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Capacity plan; fixed costs; sales assumptions; cash scenario.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Break-even progress; downside cash exposure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — Corporate cards / AP / RAY / cashflow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Costs can be surfaced; expansion profitability needs a full scenario model.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial optimization cannot decide the business strategy or discharge legal duties alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.5-10.5.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.5" target="10.5.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.5.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.5.4 · Closing a product, location or business leaves obligations unresolved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Plan outstanding deliveries, refunds, staff/vendor payments and records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Recurring charges, supplier commitments, debt and payment obligations in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Software usage, operating plans, lease/staff liabilities and closure obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritize material cash leaks and compare scenarios before committing resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Open orders; liabilities; contracts; closure tasks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Unresolved obligations; closure cost and time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — Corporate cards / AP / RAY / cashflow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Records help list obligations; complete closure execution is outside scope.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/ap-automation/&quot;&gt;F01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/blog/razorpay-agentic-dashboard-your-dashboard-just-conversational-with-ray/&quot;&gt;R01&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ramp 2/5 — Intelligence / Procurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Connects expense, invoice and purchasing controls with financial analysis.&lt;br&gt;US-led / eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/intelligence&quot;&gt;F23&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://ramp.com/procurement&quot;&gt;F24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Zoho 3/5 — Books / Inventory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Connects accounting, stock and purchasing information.&lt;br&gt;India / supported editions · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/in/books/&quot;&gt;F31&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoho.com/inventory/academy/inventory-management/real-time-management-with-zoho-inventory.html&quot;&gt;I07&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Financial optimization cannot decide the business strategy or discharge legal duties alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="3480" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.5-10.5.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.5" target="10.5.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.6" value="&lt;h2&gt;10F. Insurance and financial protection&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need to know which business losses I can absorb and which require protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Insurance purchase / renewal / financial claim support&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="4350" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.6">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.6.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.6.1 · I have no clear view of uninsured business losses&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare exposures, limits, deductibles and exclusions before choosing protection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Premiums, insured values, policy and claim status if using an insurtech.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Asset inventory, incidents, exposure, policy wording, documents and exclusions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a protection review or claim evidence pack and track outstanding steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Assets; payroll; revenue dependency; policies; exclusions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Uncovered exposure; claim-ready records; policy renewal gaps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — No dedicated merchant protection workflow verified&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No dedicated business exposure/coverage adviser was found in reviewed offerings.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 3/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;ERGO NEXT 3/5 — Commercial property insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Digital access to commercial property and covered business-income protection.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nextinsurance.com/commercial-property-insurance/&quot;&gt;F36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Insurer decisions and policy wording govern coverage; not every loss is insurable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="4350" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.6-10.6.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.6" target="10.6.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.6.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.6.2 · Policy renewals and changes in my business leave gaps in cover&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Reassess insured values and renewals when stock, staff or locations change.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Premiums, insured values, policy and claim status if using an insurtech.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Asset inventory, incidents, exposure, policy wording, documents and exclusions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a protection review or claim evidence pack and track outstanding steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Policy dates; asset values; location changes; coverage limits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Days without cover; underinsurance identified.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — No dedicated merchant protection workflow verified&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No insurance renewal and underinsurance workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 3/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;ERGO NEXT 3/5 — Commercial property insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Digital access to commercial property and covered business-income protection.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nextinsurance.com/commercial-property-insurance/&quot;&gt;F36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Insurer decisions and policy wording govern coverage; not every loss is insurable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="4350" y="1614" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.6-10.6.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.6" target="10.6.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.6.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.6.3 · A covered loss occurs but claim evidence is scattered&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Assemble financial and incident evidence and track a claim without promising a payout.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Premiums, insured values, policy and claim status if using an insurtech.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Asset inventory, incidents, exposure, policy wording, documents and exclusions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a protection review or claim evidence pack and track outstanding steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Incident records; invoices; stock values; claim status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Time to complete evidence; claim resolution time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — No dedicated merchant protection workflow verified&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Payment records can support evidence; insurance claim handling is not verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Plum 3/5 — Business insurance / benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Insurance and benefits access and administration.&lt;br&gt;India · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/business&quot;&gt;F35&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.plumhq.com/&quot;&gt;F40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;ERGO NEXT 3/5 — Commercial property insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Digital access to commercial property and covered business-income protection.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nextinsurance.com/commercial-property-insurance/&quot;&gt;F36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Insurer decisions and policy wording govern coverage; not every loss is insurable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="4350" y="2541" width="820" height="862" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.6-10.6.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.6" target="10.6.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.6.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.6.4 · Protection is offered at checkout but the cover or seller obligation is unclear&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Explain optional protection, eligibility, price and servicing responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Premiums, insured values, policy and claim status if using an insurtech.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Asset inventory, incidents, exposure, policy wording, documents and exclusions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Prepare a protection review or claim evidence pack and track outstanding steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Coverage terms; opt-in; premium; cancellations; complaints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Informed uptake; mis-selling complaints; claim friction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 0/5 — No dedicated merchant protection workflow verified&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No merchant-wide optional protection distribution workflow was verified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/&quot;&gt;R15&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Riskcovry 3/5 — Embedded insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial infrastructure fit; merchant-specific cover clarity and customer understanding still need validation.&lt;br&gt;India / supported partners · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.riskcovry.com/&quot;&gt;F42&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;ERGO NEXT 0/5 — Commercial property insurance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No direct merchant-checkout protection-distribution support identified in the reviewed commercial-property source.&lt;br&gt;US · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nextinsurance.com/commercial-property-insurance/&quot;&gt;F36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Insurer decisions and policy wording govern coverage; not every loss is insurable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="4350" y="3468" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.6-10.6.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.6" target="10.6.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.7" value="&lt;h2&gt;10G. Treasury and currency exposure&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I need spare cash to work without jeopardizing upcoming obligations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direct:&lt;/b&gt; Treasury / multi-currency accounts / finance comparison&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e5eef7;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="5220" y="380" width="820" height="220" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-root-10.7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="10.7">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.7.1" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.7.1 · Idle cash earns little but I fear being unable to pay tomorrow&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Separate operating reserves from genuinely investable surplus.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Balances, transfer timing, FX conversions and investment transactions in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Obligations, entity eligibility, risk tolerance, investment terms and currency commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Separate operational cash from surplus and compare transparent liquidity/FX scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Cleared balances; upcoming obligations; access periods; investment terms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Liquidity buffer breaches; net return after costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — RazorpayX cash views / international receipt conversion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cash visibility is adjacent; an eligible surplus-investment engine is not established.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mercury 4/5 — Treasury&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong fit for this specific pain. Cash investment and transfer workflows.&lt;br&gt;US eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mercury.com/treasury&quot;&gt;F37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 2/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Treasury products involve different risks; no universal suitability or return is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Potential product gap&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="5220" y="665" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.7-10.7.1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.7" target="10.7.1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.7.2" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.7.2 · I concentrate all operating cash with one account provider&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Monitor concentration and maintain an approved continuity plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Balances, transfer timing, FX conversions and investment transactions in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Obligations, entity eligibility, risk tolerance, investment terms and currency commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Separate operational cash from surplus and compare transparent liquidity/FX scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Balances by provider; transfer access; upcoming commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Concentration; access downtime; usable backup liquidity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RazorpayX cash views / international receipt conversion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Multi-account visibility helps; independent continuity and concentration policy remain.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mercury 1/5 — Treasury&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Cash investment and transfer workflows.&lt;br&gt;US eligible entities · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mercury.com/treasury&quot;&gt;F37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 2/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Treasury products involve different risks; no universal suitability or return is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="5220" y="1614" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.7-10.7.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.7" target="10.7.2">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.7.3" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.7.3 · Currency movements change the margin between quoting and settlement&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Estimate net exposure and compare permitted currency-conversion choices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Balances, transfer timing, FX conversions and investment transactions in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Obligations, entity eligibility, risk tolerance, investment terms and currency commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Separate operational cash from surplus and compare transparent liquidity/FX scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Invoice currencies; timing; supplier payables; quoted FX rates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Realized FX variance; margin after conversion costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 2/5 — RazorpayX cash views / international receipt conversion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Collection FX exists; comprehensive exposure management or hedging is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mercury 1/5 — Treasury&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enabling / adjacent fit for this specific pain. Cash investment and transfer workflows.&lt;br&gt;US eligible entities · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mercury.com/treasury&quot;&gt;F37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 3/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Substantial fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Treasury products involve different risks; no universal suitability or return is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fbf0d2;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="5220" y="2563" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.7-10.7.3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.7" target="10.7.3">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10.7.4" value="&lt;h2&gt;10.7.4 · I cannot compare finance products on net cost, risk and availability&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Need:&lt;/b&gt; Compare explicit fees, repayment timing, eligibility and risks on common assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fintech observes:&lt;/b&gt; Balances, transfer timing, FX conversions and investment transactions in scope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Must connect:&lt;/b&gt; Obligations, entity eligibility, risk tolerance, investment terms and currency commitments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible help:&lt;/b&gt; Separate operational cash from surplus and compare transparent liquidity/FX scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal:&lt;/b&gt; Offers; fees; cashflows; covenants; liquidity constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Measure:&lt;/b&gt; Decision errors; unexpected fees; cash shortfalls.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Razorpay 1/5 — RazorpayX cash views / international receipt conversion&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Product terms are inputs; independent cross-product suitability comparison is unverified.&lt;br&gt;India; product-specific eligibility · Confidence: Low&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/agentic-business-banking/&quot;&gt;R05&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/accept-international-payments/bank-transfers/&quot;&gt;F08&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://razorpay.com/x/corporate-cards/&quot;&gt;F02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mercury 2/5 — Treasury&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Cash investment and transfer workflows.&lt;br&gt;US eligible entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mercury.com/treasury&quot;&gt;F37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Airwallex 2/5 — Global accounts / FX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fit for this specific pain. Currency collection, conversion, transfers and accounting connections.&lt;br&gt;EU source edition / eligible global entities · Confidence: Medium&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.airwallex.com/en-eu/business-account&quot;&gt;F26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary:&lt;/b&gt; Treasury products involve different risks; no universal suitability or return is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial or uncertain coverage&lt;/b&gt; · Research hypothesis.&lt;/p&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8e2d3;strokeColor=#9eb3ab;fontColor=#173d38;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="5220" y="3512" width="820" height="884" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-10.7-10.7.4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#829b91;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="10.7" target="10.7.4">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" />
        </mxCell>
